window.PREVIEWS={"2056758487070196129":{"text":"I've joined Ostium to lead marketing!\n\nThere is a massive market opportunity ahead using blockchain rails to build better financial platforms for traders and investors globally\n\nI first met @kaledora in 2024 at Bangkok Devcon. In 2025, I visited the @ostium office where she looked me dead in the eyes and said she wanted to build a $10B company; I asked where can I send my (small) check. After a few months of learning more about the team and vision, I joined full time in March. Angel investor to employee arc activated\n\nWhat excited me most came down to the people, product, and vision:\n- The infrastructure was intentionally built to disrupt the opaque broker space and better serve digitally native traders around the world\n- Over 19m people trade CFDs, companies like IBKR are valued at $150B - market size is bigger than this channel\n- Passionate, intense co-founders that care a lot. War time mode CEO and CTO doesn't turn off. Yes, @contrarianmarco showed up in a suit in our first call\n- Getting to work with a cracked team of engineers, product developers, quants, and traders - supported by some of the best on the cap table\n- Top 20 revenue generating protocol in the whole industry\n- White glove customer service, a team focused on retention and users - @FlowTraderTM honestly needs to sleep more\n- Some more major product and partnership announcements in the works\n\nIn the last two months I've been here, we've started running growth experiments across 8+ channels, brought on two more senior growth marketers, listed sixteen new assets, revamped the liquidity engine, and announced a data partnership with a major exchange.\n\nI'm having fun and there's a lot more work to do. Looking forward to this next chapter. If you're a user, trader, or growth marketer - dms are open","date":"2026-05-19","likes":963},"2037313003591233955":{"text":"it has been fun being back in the trenches","date":"2026-03-26","likes":51,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2037313003591233955-HEX9HcEaEAANWAs.jpg"}]},"2048084717010903101":{"text":"Seeing early results with meta ads for getting new crypto users\n5.19% cvr from page visit to connect wallet\nScaling spend and optimizing landing pages now","date":"2026-04-25","likes":62,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2048084717010903101-HGxBhJoawAAhDBM.jpg"}]},"2057418674542149718":{"text":"The OrangeBox™ shoot was one of my early exposures to Fok’s creative direction\n\nTwo months ago we had these big orange boxes in the office. I was taking shots of them on the carpet thinking it’d be a good idea to tease on socials\n\nFoks came in and was like “wait what if we do something fun, like take photos of them at a bodega or something?”\n\nIn the next 45 minutes we bought a stack of newspapers, staged a setup at a bodega, and got these tasteful street shots. I downloaded some genz photo editing app to color grade it lol and boom\n\nBeyond insane taste and style Foks also comes with deep trading knowledge, is a prolific writer (he’s a huge part of our macro newsletter we send weekly), and helps sanity check copy, details, and narrative all with the utmost calm, bless","date":"2026-05-21","likes":172,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2057418674542149718-HI1rYAoXoAAuar1.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2057418674542149718-HI1rYBKX0AA9YA3.jpg"}]},"2075327476817870904":{"text":"Ostium is currently #2 in open interest right now for RWA perps. \n\nIn the last five months of being in this role, I've seen two record-breaking onchain positions. The first one was a $26m long on gold. It's pretty incredible to see blockchain rails enable people around the world to trade US markets at this magnitude. \n\nCrypto execution isn't as great as it can be (team is working on it, updates coming soon), but this is one the best places to trade metals, stocks, forex, and ETFs right now. It's not another perp dex, there's no order books to fragment liquidity. It's directly connecting traders to the underlying market which is why large size trades like this frequently happen. \n\nIf you want to test it, use code EMILY. Dms open for any feedback, asset requests, complaints","date":"2026-07-09","likes":65,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2075327476817870904-fx1.jpg"}]},"2027028027947855914":{"text":"Life update! After 4.5 years, I'm moving from CMO to a strategic advisory role at Hype. I've had a front row seat to 212+ crypto companies here and the space is now at a crossroads I want to be closer to. Institutional “adoption” is lending credibility, defi primitives have proven pmf, and AI is reshaping how we live and work. It’s been exciting to explore what this all means\n\nI'm proud to have seen Hype grow since joining in 2021:\n- Team size doubled\n- 4 awards won by our creative and campaign teams\n- 13 service lines built and running\n- 71% revenue CAGR across multiple market cycles\n- Watched talented people grow into heads of departments, VPs, and senior leaders <3\n\nThis will be an epic year for the company and clients. There's no better crypto go-to-market partner than Hype. Growth marketing and distribution is one of the most in-demand needs right now, and the team is fully primed for it. More to come soon on what the AI team has been building\n\nAs an advisor, I’ll still be contributing to launches and strategic calls. Beyond that, I’m taking space to think, learn, and go deeper on how to best build towards the future I want to live in","date":"2026-02-26","likes":680},"1989689670179942530":{"text":"Everything I’ve observed this year on crypto marketing and growth is distilled into 40 slides\n\nWe started 3+ new service lines at Hype this year. These decisions come from where my team and I see the future going and what founders are asking for \n\nTomorrow, Sunday. 3 PM. g(t)m con. Bubble Studio, Buenos Aires","date":"2025-11-15","likes":161,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1989689670179942530-D4AiXTRwX96fxIdK.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1989689540387225600/img/v2UJQeyo30TPZuGx.jpg"}]},"1961074879232430090":{"text":"Officially hit FOUR years at @hypepartners. I've seen our team double to over 100+, win two awards for crypto marketing campaigns, the development of multiple new services (paid marketing, devrel, founder branding, events, pr, short form video + two more in stealth), and have gotten to grow and learn from so many marketers and creatives these last few years \n\nWhat I'm grateful for from crypto: \n- Uncapped and unlimited learning. I've never worked in any other role longer than this one and still not bored \n- This is the best industry to work in for confluence and exposure to some of the best minds in vc, tech, ai, and finance \n- It's pushed me to voice myself more digitally, I never put intentionality into my socials for work until crypto \n- Having the opportunity to both lead and grow teams, and also learn so much from them \n- I don't know any other industry outside of DJs and touring artists that travel this much. We're so lucky to get to see each other so often in random coordinates around the world \n- It attracts some of the most eccentric, contrarian personalities and love hearing wild ideas and visions\n- I've seen it solve real world problems with capital/opportunity access, inflation hedges, payments\n- Meaning from doing work that is values-aligned. I went down the Bitcoin rabbit hole in my college dorm room 10+ years ago because of wanting the best for myself and the world around me: how do we enable more optionality, access, and sovereignty? Technological progress and ai is inevitable, how do we use and build tools that unlock ascension across facets like spirituality, health, finances, purpose? What decentralized infra can enable is one path I see towards that\n\nGrateful.","date":"2025-08-28","likes":261,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1961074879232430090-GzcZHJQXYAIEQb3.png"}]},"1920139026406719940":{"text":"CT is an echo chamber. We've been exploring organic tiktok at @hypepartners. Some stats from April for one of our clients (a crypto ai app):\n\n- 64 videos across 5 creators, pulling 2.57M+ views\n- several vids hit 90K+ views organically\n- top video has 966k views (screenshot)\n- interestingly we've tested both influencers (with existing accounts) and fresh UGC on new accounts. The top viewed video is from a fresh account \n- each creator posts consistently to build momentum\n\nConversion tracking is done via a referral link that the creator shares in comments when people ask more. We're also tracking product analytics in Amplitude\n\nWe look back to understand best hooks, openers, scripts, and double down where it's working. We're also scaling with new creators in other geos, ai models, and other channels\n\nBig W for our short form video experiments so far, led by @web3nikki (our dms are open if you'd like to test this too)","date":"2025-05-07","likes":350,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1920139026406719940-GqWyIL_XUAAxle2.jpg"}]},"1836319682611020228":{"text":"some sweet lil news: i’m moving into a cmo role at @hypepartners \n\nstands for cool memes only, send em please. Hype has mainly stayed quiet working in the trenches so I want to brag about the people and co a bit: \n- this is the 7th year existing, we’re one of the longest-standing crypto marketing agencies\n- 90ish of us, across 30+ countries, covering 12ish servicing departments on the agency side \n- about 50% of senior roles are held by women   \n- integrity and values. both from the people I work with daily like @DannyGazit_ @Jake_Stott as well as the alignment to maintain our reputation. we always strive to do our best work and only choose to work with the best builders, ecosystems, and projects\n- lowest turnover ive seen in any agency or role ive been in, speaks volumes with both how volatile crypto is and about the culture the team creates \n\ni crossed my 3 year mark last month and looking forward to do more of the same: testing the frontiers in crypto marketing, developing the best marketing talent, growing the co, sharing some learnings here, and learning myself","date":"2024-09-18","likes":768},"1809254567705497660":{"text":"Not convinced running paid ads are the way to go if you are a crypto company. If you disagree, drop screenshots of CPA and define your conversions. Please prove me wrong! \n\nI'm always willing to change my beliefs with data and to retest it with projects we work with\n\nContext: in 2021 I built up the performance marketing department at Hype. Between then and 2023, we spent $3-4 million for 30+ projects across many different channels in different conversion capacities: some awareness, some sign-ups, some purchase, etc. We immediately took opportunities to test the latest web3 ad networks, placements, and tools\n\nTableau still retains some of our learnings here in those years- not pictured: missing spends, channels missing like youtube, web3 ad networks \n\nI see some who still claim paid ads is the way to go. We haven't ran anything all year and locked in on driving community via campaign lore with built in growth loops, kols, partnerships, and organic content\n\nI started my whole career in performance marketing, I still do it on the side (I love data-driven marketing, sue me)\n\nBut frankly, if an agency, consultant, marketer is telling you you need to do paid ads, that might be wrong. Comment or dm to sense check with me if someone is. Yes, I will give you free advice.\n\n**fine print, if you are targeting web2 users, go for it. I see use cases for the big CEXs driving sign-ups. Or for those selling  goods (ecom) for example. Anything onchain needs to be abstracted","date":"2024-07-05","likes":55,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1809254567705497660-GRvAImuWwAA0ozb.jpg"}]},"1719284275059564970":{"text":"After building 20+ custom reporting dashboards and advising 35+ web3 companies on analytics, these are the 3 reasons I've found on why tracking in web3 growth is so difficult. \n\n1/ NO ONE SIZE FITS ALL \nIn Web2, there are staple measurement and tracking tools: \n\nWeb: Google Analytics, Matamo, Posthog\nMMPs: Branch, Appsflyer \nProduct: Amplitude \nEcom Attribution: Hyros, Triple Whale \n\nThen there are tools like Segment, Tableau, Domo to combine all sources and visualize together. \n\nIn Web3, we have 100+ wallets, 20+ chains with over $100m TVL, and numerous product categories that require different measurement models.\n\nProduct categories here can include:\nExchanges - cex/dex\nDefi protocol \nEcom with hardware wallets \nMarketplaces \nEcosystems \nEvents \nSocial \nGaming\nBasically web3 is the \"new internet\" right? So every product category in web2 can exist here as well. \n\nJust like Web2, each of these product categories come with all these other variables like web page, web app, mobile app. \n\nNow combine that with all the wallets, chains, multiple contracts, web2 native data, and you can see how resource-intensive and custom a winning solution for a web3 company can be. \n\n2/ TOOLING CAN'T KEEP UP \n\nEvery new chain requires tools to adapt. EVM is easiest, but imagine Cosmos and dapp chains. Or when a new chain pops up. Theres 100 chains out there with $2.5M tvl. \n\nThen, some protocols like staking pools or dexs have multiple smart contracts, on multiple chains, each requiring custom-builds from tools to adapt to. The easiest project to track is a single smart contract evm, with a wallet connect. But this is not always the case. \n\nThis is expensive and developer-intensive. Especially in a time where funding might be running slim on both the brand side, and tooling set side, and an audience crunch in the market. \n\n3/ NATURE OF BLOCKCHAIN & PRICE SPECULATION\n\nEverything lives on the blockchain, forever, but consider Inflows /outflows come from CEXs, bridges, p2p which means you lose can lose the flow of funds at some point. You also can lose entry/outflow points on the web2 side. Say someone clicks through a newsletter to to a crypto casino. You can combine that user's web2 data an click to the signup on the casino. But then they fund the wallet with Binance, and they outflow back to Binance. You have no way to track what this customer has done onchain before or after. So you're back to building an audience segment based off the web2 data points. \n\nOn top of that, even if you do use wallet analytics to segment users, I believe the main narrative of the space is purely speculative. Most of the volume and holdings in one's wallet is based off price goes up, not interest (e.g. If i buy a game NFT I might be buying it because I think it will appreciate in value, not because I'm a gamer)\n\nThis combined with a small audience (600k active wallet addresses on L2s and ETH according to Dune, + consider 1 unique user may have multiple addresses) sets us up for dismal data sizes to make coherent judgments\n\nHOW TO MANAGE? \n- Don't dismiss web2 data. Email, socials, engagement, entry points. \n- Map out your flow first, find measurement and tracking tools that can capture the priority parts of this journey \n- Use blended metrics if needed, we use this all the time in web2, especially with GDPR and Apple's notorius iOS 14 change in privacy and online ads \n- Personalize and customize. The 20+ dashboards we built for clients were each different. To measure successfully and effectively for growth, you need to tailor it to your flow","date":"2023-10-31","likes":53,"thread":[{"text":"OH and just realized I didn't even mention questing and all the engagement that can happen on another third party platform and data loss between the wallet connects"}]},"1693867097288311214":{"text":"Some slides from one of our top secret workshops at Hype HQ last week\nHow to get creativity flowing?\nDraw four circles and take 5 minutes to transform them to anything you want\nThis is what happened:","date":"2023-08-22","likes":9,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1693867097288311214-F4HTJH-XgAAHED2.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1693867097288311214-F4HTJH4W4AAV7he.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1693867097288311214-F4HTJH9WkAACQ0I.jpg"}]},"1664344705256005677":{"text":"Insane week at Hype\n- a nft drop  (mint sold out)\n- a token launch (1mm+ tokens now staked)\n- launched new in-house tool (450 users joined)\nIn full-nerd mode over here digging into the insights","date":"2023-06-01","likes":24},"1620539337443266560":{"text":"How to use data to supercharge your community:\nOur latest data dashboard built at Hype for one of our Web3 clients is straight 🔥\nImagine Sprout + Google Analytics + Dune had a baby\nIt pulls in organic social, discord, website behavior, paid marketing, dev acquisition","date":"2023-01-31","likes":17,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1620539337443266560-Fn1KgcNX0AEEZiG.png"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1620539337443266560-Fn1L6H8XoAAA1u3.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Whether you are the CMO, social media manager, or growth marketer, data is powerful when used well.\n1. Quickly identify what channels and messaging is driving community growth\n2. Spot spikes + drops to adjust messaging, spend, channels\n3. See period over period growth"},{"text":"If you have data that can answer these questions quickly, you can make sharper marketing decisions:\nWhat tweets drove the most followers?\nWhere are devs building finding you?\nWhat campaign is driving most Discord growth?\nWhat caused that spike in wallet activity?"},{"text":"No Web3 project or ecosystem is built or measures the same. We have created custom dashboards for L1s, hardware wallets (ecom), DApps, NFT projects, and much more.\nEach dashboard had to be personalized\nReach out if you'd like one made and tailored for your project."},{"text":"Oh and this one is the V2 draft, next phase coming in 1-2 weeks will include on-chain data 😎"}]},"1516415055700840449":{"text":"Very proud of our crypto paid marketing team\n- paid ad spend has 7.5x since the start of Q1\n- we’ve successfully ran crypto ads across 7+ channels\n- the department has doubled in size\n- verticals expanded from L1s and DeFi to P2E, hardware, exchanges and NFT, Web3 education","date":"2022-04-19","likes":13,"thread":[{"text":"This is a well-known (or soon to be 😉) blockchain who never ran paid marketing before\nTook them to 31mm+ impressions (targeting USA and EMEA) in a matter of two weeks across 6 channels\nBar graph shows CPM decreasing while impressions increasing DoD","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1516415065582600199-FQtjdlXaUAM1xG0.jpg"}]},{"text":"Want to join in on the fun? @hypepartners is still hiring, shoot me a DM or check out the site for all open roles!"}]},"1491084237461950468":{"text":"Sneak peak of our in-house dashboard at Hype Partners 👀\nWe're able to aggregate CPMs, CTRs, and more across our web3/blockchain clients and see trends shift over time!\nNext steps..\nBuilding connectors for Discord/Telegram\nPorting in more channels","date":"2022-02-08","likes":11,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1491084237461950468-FLFkpVBXsAUsf-x.jpg"}]},"1453004768427794438":{"text":"Hype Academy Update:\n• 250+ applications\n• 40+ countries\n• 42% WOMEN!\n• 25 selected to become web3 marketers (roughly 10% acceptance rate)\nFirst cohort starts today! Follow @hypepartners to get updates for the next cohort.","date":"2021-10-26","likes":2},"1947670385282937245":{"text":"What i was doing when i was a CMO and marketer outside of crypto: \n- channel-mix strategy \n- revenue projections \n- marketing budgets/pnl \n- negotiating with vendors\n- hiring channel and/or creative specialists \n-working with product and/or logistics team (if physical) \n\nAs a CMO and marketer in crypto? Post on x. \n\nLol jokes. but in web2, all focus was on revenue and profit. this means knowing cacs, aovs, ltv, new product lines, planning offers, best markets, costs. Both to get new customers and retain them. These retained customers *could* become a community... think loyalty programs and all. Unlike crypto, community isn't always first in web2 (although there is a slight shift now with short form and attention markets and how new dtc companies start with community first). I never built a \"personal brand\" in my entire 5+ year career in web2 because it wasn't a huge differentiating lever for UA like other efforts I could put my time into. I only started when i went full time in this industry 4 years ago. \n\nIn crypto, marketing is community-first because most GTM here is narrative and belief based, later validated by financialization. That means trust is important. We're now entering a new stage where most know it's harder to extract from markets with narrative only. So it's means going back to fundamentals, apps, things people want to use. I'm excited to see regulation put builders at ease, more crypto-abstracted apps come in, and more interest from retail (even via institutions) overall. Feels like wins for builders, users, and marketers, especially those who came from web2. Also if you're building an crypto-abstracted consumer app or tradfi on crypto rails, let's talk. Those are the two bets I've been making this year.","date":"2025-07-22","likes":291},"2061766961957126296":{"text":"“Distribution is everything” comes down to: \n\n- onboarding the right influencers/creators\n- nailing affiliate marketing \n- effective media buying\n- building owned media channels \n- having referral growth loops \n\n…and doing this all with strong and sustainable unit of economics\n\nConsumer crypto marketing is just consumer marketing now.","date":"2026-06-02","likes":398},"1986361124619464735":{"text":"Neobanks as a “new”meta brings me back to 2020 when I ran many performance marketing ads for these\n\nCACs back then: \n$7-12 app download \n$49-55 signup and KYC \n$90-120 to go through full funnel and use actual feature like cash back / payment advances \n\nThese were (centralized) fintech apps that allow you borrow, invest, earn, and bank: the same USP as many crypto neobanks today. Usually with a slick ux that is geared towards gen z/young millennials  \n\nCompetitors would be apps like Robinhood, Dave, Earnin, Cash App. We’d constantly compare landing pages and creative","date":"2025-11-06","likes":177},"1863936066782462305":{"text":"Part of my lore is I worked in a mall in a b-tier american city at 16\nThen car sales and door-to-door sales at 20\nSo i know not to underestimate the people on tiktok and fb groups saying “when (ticker) dips, the buying frenzy will be nothing short of biblical”","date":"2024-12-03","likes":90},"2016465006255108176":{"text":"oops i did it again (went viral on tiktok)","date":"2026-01-28","likes":86,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2016465006255108176-G_vrnQTXAAAwKXi.jpg"}]},"2016498527124271199":{"text":"thanks didn’t expect it with this video actually, was just a simple “oh let me click post” and the next day I woke up and it had 1 million views lol","date":"2026-01-28","likes":0},"2013685120683631051":{"text":"I definitely find X algorithm's to be more predictable (even more validated with the github repo making it open source today) but I do agree TikTok and IG Reels feels like a lottery machine pull each time \n\nIt makes sense why high-volume UGC works so well for us there for growth and impressions. Doing the same thing here would spam and give you a negative signal \n\nEven playing around with TikTok as a personal experiment \n- First DJ post goes viral, lets try 3 more - yet diminishing returns each time \n- Randomness in what goes viral /doesnt \n- Doesnt seem to make a difference with gap frequency of posting","date":"2026-01-20","likes":3,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2013685120683631051-G_ILxSmXEAEk0WD.png"}]},"2015758611205521633":{"text":"CLIPPING: crypto marketers are just discovering what it is. Here's a breakdown and how it's used for growth\n\nThe purpose of clipping is to get your video content distributed at scale. \n1. You attract editors and creators via your own pages (like the crypto marketers we're seeing now) or use existing networks or platforms like Whop\n2. Drop a brief and video/folder of content to editors and creators\n3. They find the best parts of the video and make short form clips \n4. They upload that to different sites like Tiktok, X, Youtube, etc\n\nYou then pay based on how much reach and virality the video gets.\n\n- Typical payouts are $2-5 CPM with some caps. This mean you pay $2-5 per every 1000 views\n- Although, I do see a Polymarket campaign live right now paying $0.20 CPM lol\n- Guidelines are important to set: logo visibility, caption/hashtags, how long the post should be live for, engagement % requirement, and most importantly: geos that your page targets (most split this into tiers) \n- It's a brute force action. Clippers who are successful have a sense of what could go viral from the hook, the editing, the content and then product at high-frequency \n- It's similar to our tactics for Tiktok and IG Reel growth. Post 1-3 times a day from a group of accounts and adjust hooks until you find things that work","date":"2026-01-26","likes":215},"2014001570808041727":{"text":"Close to 3M views now for one of our crypto clients running a high volume user generated video (ugc) strategy across tiktok and ig, full receipts here \n\n> been testing for the last 90 days, but things really took off in the last 30 \n> once we found a winning hook and video, we shared it with other creators and reposted on other channels \n> instagram reels actually went more viral than tiktok for this client \n> once videos go viral, it creates a flywheel as everyone commenting and engaging see more videos from that creator, as well as other creators talking about the product \n> completely scaleable: both in new channels and new accounts \n> can also take winning hooks and scale with ai models (must have infra to spin up accounts in certain geos) \n> can also repurpose for organic brand page, or turn it into paid ads (which we can run for you as well) \n\nOur team has been doing this for the last 12 months, combining both tiktok algorithm expertise and crypto-nativity (important to know how to prevent restrictions, shadow bans, and also go viral in places where crypto is not sexy). Really proud seeing how this department has grown","date":"2026-01-21","likes":244,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2014001570808041727-G_MpwICWEAAk8Mh.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"How we hit the 3M views on tiktok for a crypto company - Lynn on our short form growth team goes even deeper here:"}]},"1905600033501970902":{"text":"My account didn’t really grow until last year even though I’ve been posting crypto marketing content since jan 2023 \n\nAbout a year ago I was getting 0-50 followers a months, now it’s about 800-1000+\n\nConsistency IS absolutely important. But it’s more than that. What has worked for me? \n\n- Nuanced opinions, original thoughts. If you post vanilla takes, even if every day, you’re not going to grow. People want to be entertained and/or learn. Slop will only increase with ai \n- Play. Experiment. I’ve tested threads > infographics > spaces > screenshots of data and analytics > articles > and recently it’s been more live video streams and short form video \n- Being early in a category whether that is a media category like above, a niche (e.g. data driven crypto marketing), or even series (crypto marketing roasts with my dear friend @reka_eth is already on its 7th episode) helps differentiate you as well \n\nAll of this comes from a combination of consistency + experimentation + experience \n\nSomething i don’t mention a lot is on the last one.. experience. For 6 years of my marketing career I never put intention in growing a social page. Back when online courses were hot my ecommerce friends asked why i don’t make a facebook media buying course and just sell it. It didn’t feel right at the time. It wasn’t until i started working at Hype when I put out a screenshot of our tableau dashboards. That got a little traction, and then i made an infographic of the crypto marketing funnel + loop. That got even more traction. I went full on sharing what we’ve learned at Hype as well as personal opinions on crypto marketing \n\nToday I have at least 3 of you that will see this and maybe reply (if i’m lucky). That makes me excited to learn in public too. Not just teach what i know or share what I think \n\nYou’re going to start to see more experiments whether it’s \n- me onboarding my friends \n- bringing on experts that have nothing to do with crypto \n- introducing CT to fine art painters \n- highlighting more companies via roasts, funnel breakdowns, or questions \n+ whatever else pops into my interests, i absolutely don’t plan in centuries, these things. it’s very much go with the flow  \n\nif it looks like i’m having fun, it’s because i am","date":"2025-03-28","likes":263,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1905600033501970902-GnINIJ2bsAAF7PW.jpg"}]},"2008945807089688927":{"text":"Noticing changes in X algorithm lately: \n\n> delayed reach: posts get more impressions 6-12+ hours later, it used to be more immediate\n> check your messages: discovered i have 20+ unreads bc i'm not getting notifications for \"requests\" (oops sorry, replying now) \n> algorithm sensitivity: if you click into one post on [topic] you'll see posts on that on next timeline refresh \n> seeing less crypto posts on my timeline (getting outside of crypto audience gives you more reach now) \n> replying to popular posts gets more impressions than native -and- helps you get more visibility\n> consistency matters, when you stop posting for 2-3+ days, the first one you do seems to do v poorly \n> however, posting consistently seems to also have less  consistent reach then it used to, reach seems to be more volatile now whereas it used to be more predictable\n> need to optimize for bookmarks and qts to pop off","date":"2026-01-07","likes":406},"2013625252018884637":{"text":"How to Grow: 2026 X Algo (Exact DOs & DON'TS)\n\nAlgorithm breakdowns are flooding the timelines. This will cover exactly what to DO and DON'T to grow your account. Short and sweet.\nDO: \nWrite your posts aiming for replies - end posts with genuine","date":"2026-01-20","likes":303,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2013625252018884637-cover.jpg"}]},"1942661112480125404":{"text":"The \"sponsor our dinner\" experiment was:\n- a reminder you can just do things \n- spontaneous and planned during appetizers lol\n- a sign on how content/collaborations are changing in the age of ai and information excess \n\nTotal of 30,000 impressions so far and growing \n\nThank you @OctantApp for taking the risk on us. Gratitude to @lou3ee for filming, @ktrivs for being herself, the lovely women i had dinner with:@sophiadew @reka_eth @MashaHealy @0xLaurenveggie , and everyone who supported","date":"2025-07-08","likes":232,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1942658481577717761/img/eUkqMV2gHPE_hBWZ.jpg","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1942658481577717761/img/eUkqMV2gHPE_hBWZ.jpg"}]},"1945119712859299850":{"text":"In exchange for covering dinner, this is now the most viral video the sponsor has had with almost 100k views \n\n- 857% increase in impressions \n- 1000% increase in profile visits to @ktrivs\n- @GolemFoundation and @OctantApp being talked about \n\nnever bet against girl dinner (or me when i have something to prove <3 )","date":"2025-07-15","likes":78,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1945119712859299850-Gv50EBqXYAAkUUM.jpg"}]},"1944699997406015724":{"text":"how to go viral in 92 seconds\n(i originally made this video for tik tok but going to test something else there instead)","date":"2025-07-14","likes":267,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1944699997406015724-HYXdw4yWW289KdQV.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1944699503514177536/img/7J3wWj6AhZkjr9Uo.jpg"}]},"1943294897571725758":{"text":"The fine art of engagement baiting\n\n1. Write something that makes others want to \n- correct you \n- disagree with you\n- add their own opinion \n- share \n- bookmark to read later \n- support \n- ask a question \n\n2. Which means you need to create content that \n- is actually incorrect  \n- is right and shows a new perspective \n- resonates and captivates \n- is funny \n- is novel \n- is beautifully done \n- creates curiosity \n- teaches something \n\nThe emotions it should hit on: \n- annoyance, anger, disgust  \n- connection (when they share it to flame you in a group chat or share cause it’s a funny) \n- ego and pride (to prove you’re wrong, they’re right, show their knowledge) \n- surprise, joy, delight \n- curiosity \n\nThis video below goes over my take on future of attention capture, content, and brand collabs","date":"2025-07-10","likes":308},"1911791805584093222":{"text":"Content repurposing helped my ETHDenver talk go from 150 to 80,000+ views\n\nThis is something you can do with IRL events, videos, spaces to scale your ideas and messaging\n\nOver two weeks I:\n- Teased slides the presentation with the goal to get people to show up  \n- Did the thing (hi to the 20-30 people that came) \n- Posted a short bulletpoint recap when ETHDenver posted \n- Turned it into article format \n- Cross-posted it on LinkedIn \n- Drove readers back to my personal youtube \n\nThe article unlocked an additional 80k+ views which is a massive difference than the 150 on the yt video of the presentation\n\nHere's how it looks visually zoomed out: \n\nWith each new content format (video going to article), you can also repurpose it again for extra distribution \n\n(Yes I'm doing it with this too, calling myself out) \n\nYou can also see i had the biggest spike to my lil ole youtube account which the article funneled to:","date":"2025-04-14","likes":145,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1911791805584093222-Gnn_TmvWkAEmoW2.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1911791805584093222-GnoAO0CXUAAXWuj.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1911791805584093222-GnoAhSSWUAAdZL3.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1911791805584093222-GnoA4M8X0AA4G6Q.jpg"}]},"1884203576911880259":{"text":"Growth hack: mention you and your friends have a crypto marketing cabal\nall time high impressions, a reminder:\n- how powerful fomo is\n- how we yearn for community\n- scale of distribution digitally\nwe are now past 500 members after four days, private, and invite only","date":"2025-01-28","likes":179,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1884203576911880259-GiYJKP5XUAAQYD1.jpg"}]},"1851248468620141036":{"text":"Got a lil tg group going for ai in marketing ahead of our livestream this Thursday\nLet me know if you want in","date":"2024-10-29","likes":138,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1851248468620141036-GbDwokoWwAICFJb.png"}]},"1830882164281422117":{"text":"Our telegram mini app game went live \n\nYesterday we hit a record 1.6k new users bringing us to a total of 5.5k players\n\nAsked the data team for D7s and a better chart on retention, but so far its looking good, proud of the Hype crew involved in this one\n\nFunnel: \n1. Built a character, launched Twitter \n2. Took account from 0 to 1000 followers (my intern post was about this) \n3. Launched app + telegram group, funneled followers there\n4. App has built in growth loop with referrals, rts, follows\n5. Now focused on managing the community across Twitter and Telegram\n\nNext: continual app development (new games, new features, new partners) and launching on channels outside of crypto twitter","date":"2024-09-03","likes":248,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1830882164281422117-GWiYeM5WQAQ_vXD.jpg"}]},"1826595407243202597":{"text":"I took on being an 'intern' for a client account the last 48 hours. 200+ replies later, 8 meme posts, and making 4 custom banners for community members we are here:","date":"2024-08-22","likes":244,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1826595407243202597-GVldodiXsAAVtp7.jpg"}]},"1486162765270388740":{"text":"What is running paid ads in crypto and blockchain like? 🧵\nHere are some averages, trends and learnings (some from projects in the top 100!)\nAverage CTRs\nTwitter 0.3-0.4%\nReddit 0.2-0.3%\nDisplay 0.1-0.2%\nCrypto newsletters: 0.1-0.2%","date":"2022-01-26","likes":99,"thread":[{"text":"What channels are most effective?\nTwitter: connecting with the crypto-native audience\nReddit: personal finance interests, crypto beginners\nFacebook/IG: crypto beginners, lots of scale here\nYoutube: crypto beginners, lots of scale here\nDevpost and LinkedIn: Web2/Web3 devs"},{"text":"Hands down the biggest challenge in running paid ads for crypto and blockchain projects is compliance\nAbsolutely no airdrops or token sales (although there are creative workarounds)\nWe have a list of keywords we avoid using\nGetting an ad account banned is not fun"},{"text":"Why should crypto/ blockchain companies use paid ads?\nOrganic is important, yes\nPaid allows you to amplify all these efforts in a measurable way. The two work together and community grows 📈\nRapidly and with quality\nNo purchased bots. Don’t do that, engagement will tank"},{"text":"80-90% of impressions on Twitter from our crypto clients running ads come from paid\nThe reach is huge, we need it all for eventual mass adoption\nThere’s different segments and sub segments to reach:\nCrypto newcomers/interested\nCrypto natives\nSophisticated investors/VCs\nDevs","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1486162781791342597-FJ_pK3WWUAk1zvF.jpg"}]},{"text":"What’s happening during markets being 🔴📉?\nCosts shot up on Jan 20th when things took a dump\nInfluencers get more expensive in bull markets\nThe projects that last are the ones that keep building and growing. More adoption will occur, it’s inevitable. And paid helps","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1486162791983566850-FJ_pLaUXoAErn-r.jpg"}]}]},"2032462883943051436":{"text":"If you've googled 'peptides' in the last 30 days, this one's for you.\n\nNot Medical Advice ep. 1 with hosts @emilylai and @Bonecondor on Tirzepatide.\n\nWhat should we cover next?","date":"2026-03-13","likes":44,"author":"BoysClubWorld","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/2032462883943051436-fx1.mp4","poster":"media/2032462883943051436-fx1-poster.jpg"}]},"2007479894138110080":{"text":"ALL ABOUT PEPTIDES: my results, logs, learnings, and where to start (or if you even should) \n\nIt's been one full year since I've experimented with injecting peptides. In 2025, I used:\n> Jan - Oct:  Tirzepatide (GLP-2) \n> Oct - Dec: BPC-157, CJC-1295, Ipamorelin\n> Oct - Dec: Retatrutide (GLP-3) \n> Oct - Now: NAD+ (not technically a peptide) \n> Dec: Creatine (not a peptide, but I want to talk about it)\n> Dec - Now: GHK-cu \n\nMy main motivation for injecting strange substances into myself was curiosity on how much better I could feel in this flesh vessel. Starting with tirzepatide, the idea of weight loss was a factor but I was never overweight\n\nHigh-level, the noted benefits for each are:\n> Tirzepatide: blood sugar control, appetite suppression  leading to weight loss\n> BPC-157: tissue healing, gut lining repair \n> CJC-1295: increases growth hormone which helps with muscle repair, recovery, collagen\n> Ipamorelin: synergistic with CJC-1295, also promotes growth hormone and enhances sleep, muslce recovery \n> Retatrutide: does what tirzepatide does at higher levels alongside metabolic rate increase\n> NAD+: energy and cellular repair \n> Creatine: strength, recovery, cognitive benefits\n> GHK-Cu: collagen, hair/skin growth, tissue repair\n\nNow what I actually experienced: \n\nTirzepatide: \nSince Jan 2025, I've lost 15lbs (7kg), 10% of body weight. Tirzepatide definitely contributed for this. I tested my blood in May and was -11 my biological age Inflammation was low. Beyond weight loss, what tirzepatide truly helped me with was dialing in on diet and my fitness habits. Appetite suppression is strong. You don't feel like eating but know you have to, so you opt in for whole foods, high protein, low carb etc. You also want to build muscle when you're losing weight so you lift weights. Honestly, tirzepatide was the gateway peptide lol. I went down a pant size, now had abs lol, I saw my blood panel results, and I felt great. It's why I kept experimenting. \nDosage: \n2.5 mg weekly, I titrated up to 3.5 mg ONCE (0.5mg increase each week) but then went back down to 2.5mg. Why? I had a good friend do two months of ozempic. In the prescribed pen, they have you jump dosages wildly. 2.5 to 5 to 10 etc. She forgot to eat and although she lost a lot of weight, she suffered hair loss too. \n\nBPC-157+CJC-1295+Ipamorelin: \nI put these all in one syringe. Tbh, it's hard to say if I felt any different. At this point I was already dialed in on health. I did notice my biceps being more dense but who knows if it would have already been like that because I was hitting protein goals daily. I also had less back pain but I'm not sure if that was from weight loss, inflammaton reduction, or just more upper back strength vs. this stack. I will say I did not experience differences in sleep.\nDosage: \n400mcg BCP-157, 200 mg CJC-1295, 200mg Ipamorelin daily \nCycle: \n8 weeks. Stopped. Likely won't repeat for now. \n\nNAD+\nI'm loving NAD+. I feel the benefits and see them compounding too. I feel the energy rush immediately and stay through throughout the day. I've tried NAD+ IV drips before, but injecting it subq and having consistent access has been a game changer. I noticeably see the difference with running which I track. More stamina and energy. Thinking and cognitive recall seems faster too but thinking about thinking is so meta and subjective. \nDosage:\nLoading period of 100mg daily for 10 days. Then 2-3x a week 100mg each. Now I'm at 50mg 2x a week. \n\nRetatrutide: \nTirzepatide got me to a weight level I was happy with yet I was curious about retatrutide, the next evolution of GLPs. The main benefit I'm seeking now is inflammation reduction (look into liver fat reducton).I recently stopped however because it was causing some gastric stress. I noticeably felt it when doing a 72 hour zero-cal 1.5 weeks ago. My whole digestive track was immensely slower.. even with no food in my body. The fast has made it easy to move to intermittent fasting on a 16:8 window, and I'm considering just keeping it at that. Reta seemed to have less of appetite suppression than tirzepatide for me, but it could also be that I'm taking a tiny dose and my body is accustomed now. One risk of this one is there are reports of higher heart rate at high dosages. \nDosage: \n0.5mg-1mg weekly, a microdose basically. If I start again will surely be 0.5mg\n\nCreatine: \nThere's a cult-like following around creatine to a point where I felt gaslit when trying to find information online on why it made my face so puffy. I did it for 30 days, drank lots of water. Felt great at the gym but tbh no wild noticeable difference. Stopped it during my fast and saw my cheekbones get more snatched so decided to stop all together. \nDosage: 3mg daily. No loading. \n\nGHK-Cu: \nOk honestly my skin is pretty damn great as it is but I had two vials of this and just started out of curiosity. Not sure if it's making a difference or will, but will do a full cycle and see. \nDosage: 1mg daily, will cycle for 8 weeks.\n\nOther notes to call out: \n- It's hard know if any single input (outside of tirzepatide and NAD+) made a difference because my habits changed over the year, and I'm also mixing this with other modalities.. \n- I don't drink alcohol. Haven't for 12+ years\n- Fully sober\n- I sleep, have a grandma schedule lol\n- First Vipassana in April, started meditating daily since more or less \n- Burned out, nervous system disregulated in July/August \n- Tested 11 years younger by blood in May (after Vipassana) and only 6 years younger by blood in November \n- After blood panel, started supplementing Vitamin D+K2+Omega3s\n- Currently taking an iron supplement with GHK-cu\n- For skin, also doing a red light mask daily since Jan 2025, this has made a difference \n- Added in daily sauna and ice bath in Dec \n^ all this context is to show I'm not sure how much is from the peptide vs. the lifestyle. But I do feel the strongest, sharpest, most spiritually aligned self I've ever been \n\nShould you take peptides? It depends on your own goals. Ultimately dialing in sleep, exercise, diet should be the baseline \n\nIf you do take them, I suggest: \n- lowest dose possible first, see how you feel then titrate up \n- stagnate them, so you can better isolate results \n- getting it from a source where they test each batch \n- doing your own research and not trusting what people say online \n\nTools I use: peppedia, reddit, gpt, some books to learn dosages and effects (then i use the lowest dose to start) \n\nSource: peptide dot partners, use EMI for 10% off \n\nLast note: I think looksmaxxing is cool and all but not at the cost of spirit loss. This whole experience taught me aesthetics is easier than ever to obtain. Even before the peptides craze there was botox/fillers and just wearing all-black tailored clothes. Being hot is not just a conscious choice but it's currently at the lowest barrier to entry than ever before. This makes it way less impressive. \n\nWhat's going to actually matter isn't how you look, but how you feel, and make others feel.","date":"2026-01-03","likes":1101},"2014398183560851650":{"text":"UPDATE ON PEPTIDES TESTING (pt 2) - Ok I think so I've hit peak female performance tbh, never felt better. All about my multi-year relationship to \"biohacking,\" health, and ultimately: feeling as good as I possibly can\n\nThe original post goes into peptide testing for the last 12+ months and my current philosophy on health. Start there if you haven't read anything yet (none of this is medical advice, just my own personal experiences) \n\nThis is a basic tracker I use in Google sheets, you can see everything I'm doing now. \n\nSome updates since that post has gone viral: \n1. I was influenced and got back into creatine \n2. About to hit 30 days of GHKcu (copper peptides that are meant for skin generation, collagen, lowering inflammation: half way through this testing cycle) \n3. Updates on my other habits and their impact \n4. Started retatutride again, trying a split microdose 2x a week \n\nOn my last post, I realized I didn't mention a few things about the peptides: \n- For compounded peptides in powder form, you do need to reconstitute it with BAC water \n- There are peptide calculators online to know how to do this and amounts based on dosage \n- You'll also need needles and alcohol pads, I usually use 31g for needles, they're tiny and smol \n- They do need to stay refrigerated after reconstitution, i usually carry mine in this handy little bag you see above when I travel, or prep into syringes with an ice pack \n\nUpdates: \nI was re-influenced to take creatine again.  \nI stopped initially because it was making my face so bloated and I hated the look. ONE girl friend and many men talked up the positive effects. One most intriguing to me was cognitive effects. I also noticed needing more recovery time so I decided to pick it up again and I started with a heavier loading period - 6-10g a day vs. just 3g. The weekend I started I was snowboarding. The main difference outside of loading heavier dosages was I drank insane amounts of water - like 4L a day. I woke up and would drink 1.5L with electrolytes. The ski stations in Europe have toilets everywhere, bless. I am actually now 15 days in on creatine and take it more intuitively. On days I know I'm going to run and lift a lot, I might do 6g. On lighter days I'm doing 3g. I think 4L was way too much water from how much I had to use the bathroom and now mainly aim for 2.5-3L. The biggest thing is I'm not experience facial bloating anymore!! And I definitely feel recovery time improved. I snowboarded three days in a row and usually my quads burn out. They were sore but I had more stamina this season than the last 2-3 years. Not sure if cognitive effects are here but I feel generally sharp anyways, curious if it'll get better when I hit the month mark. Keeping it up now\n\nSpeaking of recovery times, I got into running. \nNAD+ is still being injected at 50mg twice a week. I'm not sure how much of it is contributing to stamina but something shifted December and I went from getting tired at 10-15 minutes to easily doing 20 and now doing 30 minutes daily. It's meditative at this point. I'm do 4-5km a day before work, after my vipassana meditation. I was in Paris last weekend and I saw my TCM guy (highly recommend you get one, he clocked me on eating too much fat - I blame that fondue). He knew I started running just going over my foot, legs, hips. Apparently for my body I need to super well cushioned shoes and to do shorter strides so I'm working on that now. \n\nThis chart is actually shocking. I can't believe I gaslit myself into enjoying running. Like wow the human mind is so powerful\n\nIntermittent fasting for 27 days now. \nI also run fasted. After my 3 day zero calorie fast, I moved to a daily intermittent fasting window of 16 hours fasting, 8 hours eating. It's actually easy to maintain when you eat a high protein, low carb diet. The only thing to call out here about that is earlier this week I ate way too much fat (i bought 3kg of pili nuts) and actually threw up. I pushed my body too deep into a ketosis or something too fast lol. It's a lot easier to detox however when you eat less which fasting (and GLPs) do, because you're giving your gut a break\n\nMy exact morning looks like this right now: \n1. Wake up \n2. Meditate (i do vipassana - basically a body scan and feeling sensations) \n3. Creatine, black coffee sometimes \n4. Run for 30 mins/5km \n5. Gym and lift \n6. Sauna for 20 minutes, 80C, sometimes ice bath (intuitive) \nWork. Break my fast. \n\nOn the sauna and ice bath. \nSo I read that super long post by Bryan Johnson on how great the sauna is. It's another moment for me to meditate and recover after lifting and running. \n\nSomething I laugh to myself about as I'm inside sweating out supposed microplastics is how much longevity advice I'm taking from someone who tells me to \"protect my swimmers.\" I think for women, for me at least - my views on \"biohacking\" are not for increased ROI or output (they used to be at one point), nor to live forever (sounds like a curse ngl), it's more to feel as fcking good as I can which means: closer to my spirit, clearer mind, purer heart, more energy, more creativity. So I do things intuitively too, like with the creatine dosage. On certain parts of my cycle, I might not do the ice bath or change what I eat that day. But I will say I've been sauna-ing daily for 33+ days or so now, with 6 days off when I went to the alps and Paris, and it's felt great. Ice bath a lot less. \n\nRetatutride: split microdose 2x a week \nI hit my goal weight a few months ago, but was curious to try the latest GLP on a tiny dose for inflammation reduction. I stopped for a bit because it was giving me gastric issues. I started again after my 3 day fast combined with intermittent fasting and clean eating. The other thing I'm testing is splitting the dose 2x a week. I'll need to realistically take a blood panel test to know the effect because theoretically, intermittent fasting should be lowering inflammation too. I will say though this round has been much better on my stomach outside of my time in France when I overdid it on cheese and the overconsumption of pili nuts. I don't necessarily feel appetite suppression but I also don't really need it atm as I have this eating window that's quite easy to adhere to. On weight - I've actually gained 2 more pounds but not too worried as I'm focused on building strength and muscles. Going to do a pull up this year. \n\n30 Days of GHKcu\nSo my skin has been pretty phenomenal for the last 12 months. It could be the red light mask, or my skincare products, or my water intake. GHKcu is a \"beauty peptide\" touted by many women so I was curious how much better it could skin get. It actually got worse lmao. \n\nPhoto of me in November before I started and what I sent the group chat on Day 18:\n\nBUT - I'm now on Day 29 or so and I think it actually is improving? My skin feels softer. I noticed this earlier this week. Who knows if it's the running and sauna (excessive sweating) or the GHKcu. I also increased the dose to 2mg and will complete this cycle and see. My hair has always grew fast so not seeing a huge difference there. Probably also can see something if I do a blood panel test but hard to attribute. \n\nWhen I say I feel like I hit peak female performance, I mean that I've never felt healthier, fit, and spiritually aligned. Having a clearer mind also makes me feel more creative, funnier, kinder. (I could be so off base though lol). Something else I've noticed that helps is clocking myself in my daily meditation and running on how my nervous system is. Some days it's easier to sink into the body and sensations than others. I know I didn't sleep well or move excess energy/stress out if I'm stuck in the mind layer. I feel pretty damn good these days but I'm interested in testing Semax (for cognitive benefits) and Tessamorlin (apparently more effective than CJC + Ipamorelin for hgh/muscle growth). Since it's getting harder to attribute what input is creating the effect, I'll likely do these when I'm done with certain cycles.\n\nLong term habits to keep: \n- Sleep consistently \n- L-theanine + magnesium glycinate before bed \n- 16:8 intermittent fasting daily \n- High protein, low carb \n- Running, lifting, sauna \n- Creatine \n- Red light mask for face \n- NAD+ \n- Meditate \n- Alcohol free for life\n- Not smoking or vaping for life \n\nShort-term/testing: \n- Retatutride \n- GHK-cu \n- Tessamoralin (will stop GLPs before I start this, when/if I do) \n- Semax \n\nWant to iterate what i said in my last post that with \"looksmaxxing\" and longevity becoming commoditized -  being hot (outwardly) is easier than ever. That's going to become a lot less interesting. Especially on the digital layer where you can just nano banana yourself now. The way I look at health is how can I feel the highest frequency version of myself that makes me the most creative, kind, and at ease - which I believe also affects the people I care most around me. None of this is medical advice, consult a doctor <3","date":"2026-01-22","likes":466,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2014398183560851650-G_STzdjXAAAYl1a.png"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2014398183560851650-G_SUAo8WkAEm-e_.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2014398183560851650-G_SUILgXgAExbsD.png"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2014398183560851650-G_SUZmJWQAEca6j.jpg"}]},"2015443330742521904":{"text":"Was asked how much this all costs. Currently:\n1. Reta, NAD+, GHKcu: $96.2/mo\n2. Gym + sauna: $95.5/mo\n3. Creatine: $12.45/mo\n4. Running: free baby \n\nAll costs for peptides used in past: \nTirzeptide: $33.32/mo\nRetatutride: $17/mo\nNAD+: $38.4/mo\nGHK-cu: $40.8/mo\nBPC-157: $46.8/mo\nCJC-1295: $50.4/mo\nIpamorelin: $50.4/mo\n\nOf course, depends on source, dose, frequency (none of this is medical advice)","date":"2026-01-25","likes":454},"2032563549935992921":{"text":"The very first episode of Not Medical Advice is here.\nBirb and I go over our 12+ months of Tirzepatide logs, what seems to be the gateway peptide and chatGPT’s most asked about GLP:","date":"2026-03-13","likes":20,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2032563549935992921-HDUdxcHWsAE2bH_.jpg"}]},"2057796161797325052":{"text":"Cold brew in a wine glass. Russian analog cognitive peptides.\nReady for The Great Lock In.","date":"2026-05-22","likes":87,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2057796161797325052-HI7CstVW0AABHCr.jpg"}]},"2052325841271407099":{"text":"Update: took a blood panel last week and now my phenotypic age is ~18\nStarting to think this calculation is as accurate as doing aura photography lol","date":"2026-05-07","likes":25,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2052325841271407099-HHtTeZDXEAIZt5d.jpg"}]},"1998475580249981019":{"text":"I took two blood panel tests this year. Tested 24.3 in biological age last month. Thought this was excellent, ego was uplifted \n\nThen i plugged in my results from may when i was fresh out of a 10 day meditation silent retreat. I was biologically 19. Biomarkers show i'm gen z, but wow... aging five years in seven months is horrendous lol","date":"2025-12-09","likes":114},"1919048359899287685":{"text":"for any other health nerds or people into biohacking, i had 3 IV drips and did a blood test this week lol… what i learned and felt \n\nfirst, i thought if i’m here in dubai where you can literally press a button on an app and they come to your hotel, why not? plus a few events had them, values aligned \n\nduring each iv drip i didn’t feel anything during nor felt any different after\n\npeople: “how do you feel?”\nme: “exactly the same” lol \n\nanyways im all for this concept of shooting up all vitamin cocktails that hopefully does something, and if not, maybe i benefit from the placebo \n\n> tuesday: immunity drip at sophon crypto detox \n> friday: \n∙ blood test in morning\n∙ 100mg nad+ in afternoon\n∙ c24 (ton of vitamins and amino acids) at berabaddies in evening \n\nmy lifestyle: i don’t drink, smoke, weight lift (but failed to do this all week), aim for bed by 11 pm at conferences (but also failed towards last 3 days cause i get stressed making keynotes) \n\nwhat was the most interesting was the blood test which went over like 50+ biomarkers \n\ni took the pdf and plugged it into gpt and had it rate me \n\nlong story short, crypto conferences wear me down. my cortisol (stress) was upper normal by the end of the week. i’m low on vitamin d and apparently a lot of us are? so will start supplementing. also i need to eat more meat, i tried being veg for 14 days since the ten day vipassana meditation but yeah iron levels are not looking good so i had a ton last night at hot pot as my last meal in dubai which honestly fixed me \n\nhighly recommend doing this for yourself, it’s fun learning what’s happening in the body. health is wealth. and also chill out and disconnect because this industry is chronically online and stimulated \n\ni had a great time meeting those i managed to see in dubai, sorry if i could barely talk yesterday i was slowly crashing out inside. if we missed each other let’s find some time soon :)","date":"2025-05-04","likes":53,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1919048359899287685-fx1.jpg"}]},"1641095312046530570":{"text":"Hack for better sleep and waking up recharged\n1. Lose your Oura Ring\n2. Make it impossible to open any sleep tracking apps\n3. Enjoy a peaceful morning without any anxiety on if your REM/HRV was worse or better","date":"2023-03-29","likes":9,"thread":[{"text":"🤣","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1641095431881891846--_8HfFl7oPQUfy0_.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1641095314122653699/img/aFidFltTngGzJFtf.jpg"}]}]},"1406472228791668742":{"text":"I’ve stopped wearing my Oura ring after 3 years\nSomething about going back to basics has been resonating with lately\nI’ve used the tech as a tool to prove the natural (sun, nutrients, exercise) can help improve sleep and HRV, so cycle complete. Let it go","date":"2021-06-20","likes":2},"1272237327285399552":{"text":"Insane amount of deep sleep the last two days: 3+ hours...\nOnly change was taking vitamin D (5000UI) + K (90mcg)","date":"2020-06-14","likes":9,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1272237327285399552-EaflGnAXgAEJPln.jpg"}]},"1299081302998687758":{"text":"If you're reading this, stand up, do some chin tucks, strengthen your core, throw your computer out the window, blend your phone for fun, hug a stranger, go to a 90 day yoga retreat, never sit down again\n That's my neck on the right 😭","date":"2020-08-27","likes":192,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1299081302998687758-EgdCgvbWAAAdd3u.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Plan of action cause this is probably you too in some degree\n- Chiropractor adjustments\n- Lay on a denneroll pillow for 15 minutes daily\n- Strengthen core, upper and lower back\n- Lots of chin tucks"}]},"2001729720497369172":{"text":"update on tech neck 5 years later… vastly improved mainly from changes i made this year. initially, i was doing chiropractor visits and laying on a dennerolle daily. it helped, but didn’t maintain \n\ni saw photos of myself when I started speaking on stages in 2024 and was like “ooof i need to fix that posture” lol and started building upper back muscle","date":"2025-12-18","likes":2372},"2001730882554728506":{"text":"lost weight and built back muscle mainly\ni also do accupuncture in my neck area to release tension but this is more relief than anything\nI’ll send you the video of the exact exercises I do on tg :-)","date":"2025-12-18","likes":68},"2011411568404128221":{"text":"Grew an inch in the last five years: 2021 vs. 2026\nSimply:\n- Lost weight\n- Built back muscles (important!!)\n- Became v conscious of posture","date":"2026-01-14","likes":185,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2011411568404128221-G-n3MORbcAIII7K.png"}]},"2011437813774844141":{"text":"In 2020 i noticed a lump in my upper back and that started me off with going to a chiropractor and getting the xrays you see in the original post lol\nThen in 2024 when I started speaking on stages I noticed my posture in videos/photos and was like ok.. we gotta fix that","date":"2026-01-14","likes":0},"2011484778957099206":{"text":"yeah there’s three my physio showed me\nthen i do a lot of rows and working on pull ups now!!!","date":"2026-01-14","likes":1,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2011484778957099206-G-o6veWWYAAA7s-.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2011484778957099206-G-o6ve3bQAUM55a.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2011484778957099206-G-o6veVa4AA3Myw.jpg"}]},"2011740727798350038":{"text":"these exercises and building upper back strength help me maintain basically\nthen the rest of what I wrote - lose weight / reduce inflammation / be more conscious throughout day","date":"2026-01-15","likes":1},"2005540854778167685":{"text":"If you want to slow down time, slow down your brain \n\nBeing bored is an underrated skill in a world of increasing abundance. End of year is one of my fav times to live on 0.5x for a prolonged period\n\nToday I’ll break my 72 hour fast (a rare, if only crosspost from my ig on how I felt yesterday)","date":"2025-12-29","likes":84,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2005540854778167685-G9UcxlMXIAAC_jK.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2005540854778167685-G9UcxlFWQAE-w4q.jpg"}]},"1229215899053367296":{"text":"1. 59 hours into my first water fast! 💦 Ever done one before?\nWill update this thread as I go...\nFive days\nNo food\nNo coffee\nNo tea\nNo supplements\nJust distilled water\n(I just started adding minerals an electrolytes today)\n@zerofasting thank you for this pretty app!","date":"2020-02-17","likes":5,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1229215899053367296-EQ8NV-yXUAAJ4mv.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"2. WHY?!\nScience says:\nrebalances hormones, rebalances insulin levels, detoxes, weight loss, resets gut and improves digestion\nMy esoteric reason: it came up 3x through conversation with friends in one week.\nI have a rule that if sometime happens twice, it’s a sign"},{"text":"3. Day 1\n- Can’t eat so compensating by chugging water and having something in my mouth\n- Energy and focus is decent\n- Urge to eat or snack? Chug water  💦\n- 1 gallon finished"},{"text":"4. Day 2\n- Slept a whole 8 hours for the first time in two weeks! 💤\n- Woke up before alarm\n- Was able to focus and get some sprints in 👩‍💻\n- Face is starting to break out\n- A little less than a gallon finished"},{"text":"5. Day 3\n- Another 8 hours of sleep 💤\n- Heavily considered breaking fast, craving SALT 🍟\n- Face isn’t getting worse, but still have a breakout happening\n- Made it to yin yoga 🧘‍♀️\n- Solid focus and clear thinking\n- Pacing for less water today\n- Weighed in: 4 pounds lost 🤯","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1229215912240320513-EQ8NWiPXUAMHnek.jpg"}]},{"text":"6. Day 4 of this water fast\n- Feeling happy and great today☀️\n- Weighed in, 7 pounds down\n- Hunger is completely supressed\n- Body is heavily detoxing... I have no idea how as I haven’t put anything in it aside from water for 72+ hours now\n- Face break out is resolving","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1229526071797829632-ERAncO0WoAENfBM.jpg"}]},{"text":"7. ‼️79 Hours into water fast: BROKE FAST!\nRealizing the longer I fast, the longer it’ll take me to adjust to digestion. I fly out of NYC this week and went to enjoy some foreign foods.\nBroke fast with a cup of grassfed bone broth + an avocado 🥑","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1229538820267397120-pczh9iu5C8GzAh6J.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1229538791926444032/pu/img/r3xdDDf1BeYhFILR.jpg"}]}]},"1912921067301011567":{"text":"Hello world, experiment over. The last 10 days I had no internet, phone, laptop, could not talk anyone, read, and was completely offline \n\nEverything you saw from after this rt post until today was scheduled\n\nI gave @FelixHowes access and he was my reply girl.. I laughed at some of these replies cause some I would never say hahah but how did he do? Thank you Felix for your service\n\nWhat was i doing? Somewhere in rural romania meditating every day for ten hours, from 4:30 am until 9 pm. It was absolutely not fun, but immensely meaningful. The most exciting thing was meals (which we only had breakfast and lunch) and seeing the occasional sheep herd if it aligned with our 10 minute in between meditation break. I finally took a 10 day Vipassana course. Huge gratitude to @enaraxr for being a gift in my life and also inspiring me to gift this to myself, an absolute gift  \n\nThings I learned about X and the algo : \n- For one, there was this super dumb feeling of \"what if i spiral to irrelevance\" by not being online before I left. I disliked scheduling content and premaking content, this life isn't for me but might for work others \n- Data shows the last 10 days, all metrics were indeed red except for engagement rate\n- So there is something to be said about being chronically active which fed my ability to share takes live in the moment which do better impression wise, same with being able to reply back in the moment \n\nMore important things I learned: \n- It took me 3 full days of ten hour meditations to finally calm my brain and be able to consistently see my thoughts, being this online the way crypto demands is not healthy \n- Our brains are insane lol \n- I used to think chaos is increasing in the world but had a realization in a meditation that its the information age and having access to every issue happening at all times, anywhere, at our fingertips \n- I didn't miss my phone as much as I thought I would. I more missed my friends and family and thought of my phone as a tool to message them\n- Nothing is that deep, including this post, my x account, your x account, your tge, blah blah it's all impermanent \n- Life is for enjoying and I enjoy what I do a lot, and looking forward to going back to work (will catch up fully Monday) with more calm \n\nThe secret to peace and happiness is understanding life is full of volatility and not reacting to it. I've read a lot of spiritual books and seen workshops and logically understood it.. but Vipassana helped me truly understand on an experiential level. This was a gift and I hope one day you can take 10 days and do it yourself - it'd make crypto better as well :) \n\nThere's centers all over the world, it's all donation based, you can find one near you at dhamma dot org","date":"2025-04-17","likes":163,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1912921067301011567-GowLGfDXwAAgF6r.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1912921067301011567-GowNlslWoAA4A0D.jpg"}]},"1915691857146794021":{"text":"i’m now meditating 1-2 hours a day, taking protein, creatine, and spending more time outside without my phone\nnot sure if you’re ready for this emily arc","date":"2025-04-25","likes":246},"2095865781804302509":{"text":"Every new AMC minted onchain is a real share that had to be bought first, which means tokenized stocks drive global demand for the underlying stock \n\nIt’s like how stablecoins drive global demand for the US dollar \n\nRight now with regulations, tokenized stocks are just wrappers with fewer rights and (supposedly only) available to non US people\n\nAlpaca usually custodies them, then in Robinhood’s case they have a Jersey entity that issues them. KYB’d authorized participants mint only after the traditional shares are bought and held in custody\n\nIt should be a net positive for both AMC (and US markets) that new global audiences can now “buy” the stock","date":"2026-09-04","likes":45,"author":"emilylai"},"2090641761492168962":{"text":"Nasdaq's Director of Communications for their \"Digital Liquidity Networks\" org  role is a peek into the future: \n- continuous, always-on trading \n- programmable market structures \n- tokenization \n\nI started wondering when Nasdaq and NYSE tokenize equities, how they will execute. Will it be fragmented order books? And does it directly compete with the xStocks, Ondo stocks, Robinhood token stocks, Dinari stocks today?\n\nI looked into the SEC releases and found out both Nasdaq and NYSE are launching tokenized equities with  unified liquidity - both tokenized and traditional shares will trade on the same order book \n\nThis however, won't be DeFi. It's walled gardens, permissioned finance on crypto rails\n\nFor reaching offshore non-US people: \n- Nasdaq is partnering with xStocks (Kraken/Payward) on an equities gateway that converts DTCC custodied equities to tokenized forms\n- NYSE is launching a new 24/7 venue for tokenized securities\n\nBoth of these efforts bring flow back to the underlying US capital markets. Crypto rails create access and extend distribution to global capital, similar to stablecoins increasing demand for the dollar or Fasanara getting new investors on their Global Diversified Alternative Debt Fund with Midas. These also both seem to be competitors to existing tokenized equity options that exist today, with full defi composability - but will not merely be wrappers\n\nThere's three levels of blockchain finance emerging: \n1. Existing finance importing controlled, blockchain infrastructure (walled gardens) \n2. Permissioned DeFi: whitelisted assets, AML/KYC/KYB, for accredited investors only but usable in composable onchain markets\n3. Fully permissionless DeFi","date":"2026-08-21","likes":33,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2090641761492168962-fx1.jpg"}]},"2089442129605017805":{"text":"Been going down a rabbit hole of tokenization: stocks, asset backed securities, private credit, and money market funds.  Went through ~550k of words across panels from TokenizeThis from June, podcasts, developer docs, asset manager and vc research, and industry reports\n\nA lot of X and crypto content is self advertising, so it's hard to get unbias, objective takes. Digesting all this then pattern matching it both in aggregate and to the TradFi analog has been really helpful in my learning process.\n\n- This headline I saw yesterday reads bullish (and yes let's give the growth credit) but tokenized equity markets are extremely fragmented. Imagine the depth of $2.3B spread across 1.4M holders across 1,000+ tokenized stocks on multiple chains and frontends \n- Market makers go where flow is. Retail getting bad slippage means less flow, which means worse slippage. Chicken and egg situation \n- Tokens trade 24/7 but the underlying stock market is closed on weekends, creating even worse liquidity and gap risks\n- Robinhood and Binance (bStocks) seem to be leading retail front for tokenized equities which makes sense, they have distribution to the end user. Distribution is harder than issuance, all the tech rails exist today \n- Most X posts will look at the growth of tokenized stocks via issuance: xStocks vs. Ondo vs. Robinhood etc, but not many mention how nearly all go through one broker and clearer: Alpaca, the real winner here\n- Alpaca and Oracles seem to have the best monetization models in this, effectively being the bridge in bringing TradFI onchain and pricing it\n- Tokenized stocks have multiple legal variants with a spectrum of actual rights to just exposure: Jersey debt certificates, BVI total-return notes, ADGM certificates all giving a different range of rights to just pure exposure\n- Tokenized private credit is interesting, I still need to read more... the underlying loans never trade so there's no market price yet oracles push a NAV from some fund admin on a schedule while DeFi works 24/7\n- Institutional tokenized products have massive (inflated) TVLs compared to tokenized equities right now. DeFi composability creates real yield opportunities (lev looping a tokenized CLO or MMF) yet they're typically permissioned with minimums and KYB\n\nA lot of the future for more capital efficient onchain markets comes down to regulatory clarity. Will be interesting to see DTCC rolling out it's tokenization commercial launch in Oct, Nasdaq and NYSE moving forward with their tokenization roadmaps, and SEC possibly rescinding rule 611, making it easier for public equities to be traded on blockchain rails","date":"2026-08-17","likes":53,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2089442129605017805-fx1.jpg"}]},"2081663181441597879":{"text":"Been on an absolutely streak with RWA markets (facebook marketplace) lately, great place to learn about market microstructure dynamics \n\nBid/ask spread: i know i’m going to get negotiated on \n\nLiquidity: how fast or slow something sells \n\nPrice discovery: when i have to lower the ask price \n\nSpoofing: getting ghosted after agreeing lol \n\nCounterparty risk: settlement and safety: is it cash? is it real? will the revolut tx land instantly?\n\nAnyways, i’m selling a ton of my glasses, i accumulated way too many and don’t like what i’ve become","date":"2026-07-27","likes":61},"2095453564902461921":{"text":"Set up my grok bot ferny with it's own virtual card and it booked flights and emailed a calendar invite for me \n\nPretty magical","date":"2026-09-03","likes":22,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2095453564902461921-fx1.jpg"}]},"2094042611589783950":{"text":"Day 8 with grok @bot, everything i've used it for: \n\nTrip planning:\n- One bot is actively monitoring flights and pinging me when it's at a certain price \n- Plan out visas: how to apply, where to go, costs, best agencies and reminding me \n- Sending emails to check if stores have a specific product and making reservations for me\n- Searching and building out itineraries then adding it to my calendar \n- Created a tableall account and made lists of sushi restaurants to go to in Japan \n\nDaily life and errands: \n- Adding events to my calendar or reminding me things I need to do at a certain day or time \n- Researching best products and checking all forums, reviews, and cheapest websites to get it from, including finding coupon codes\n- Canceling free trials for me before I get charged lol\n- Daily brief of AI + Tech + Crypto news \n\nWork: \n- Going through onboarding flows and doing full UX and messaging reviews for me \n- Designing websites \n- Doing due diligence on companies and the people behind them (it searches their LinkedIn, news, any press, confirms numbers) \n- Designing and coding a new website\n- It helped me write this post \n- Auditing work done by other LLMS\n\nMy current team set up: \n1. Big boss bot: the main one i interface with that delegates to all the other bots, sets up routines and reminders\n2. Deep researcher: does a lot of the research, looks on X and web, fact checks\n3. CMO: does a lot of marketing strategy, copy, analysis, positioning and growth \n4. CTO: anything technical, related to code, ai setup  \n5. Therapist: my brainstorm buddy, will ask me questions \n\nI've also had big boss bot read @ericzakariasson 's share of all the grok bot guides and intake that for the others, added @poteto 's pstake skill, her dr egg bot template which helps make new bots (i used this to also train the existing bots), and @heyrobinai 's alfred template which did an audit of how all the bots are working together\n\nI'm finding myself using grok bot for my day to day more than Hermes, mainly out of token usage, but I have them sharing the same brain. I also found grok dot com is better for fuller reports using real-time X. @claudeai is still my main driver for a majority of coding and dense research (you can only attach 6 files to grok bot at time and cannot choose model)","date":"2026-08-30","likes":86,"author":"emilylai"},"2092731640749473861":{"text":"I fed an agent skills on CRO, positioning, user journeys and then had it go through the entire flow for EtherFi\n\nIt captured screenshots and dropped it into miro with a full assessment on what to keep, change, cut. Next steps here are to tune the skills and train the agent further based on this initial output \n\nThe world of doing this at scale is here. You can also give an agent a designated iphone so it can do this for mobile apps, equip it with a pw management system, and it's own capped virtual card to make payments. Pretty cool\n\nAlso thank you to @tysonwynne_ for hooking me up with pinnacle tier. I think @etherfi is the only verticalized crypto card product right now where one can borrow USDC, leverage loop onchain CLOs, and spend against it lol. my link if you want to test it out: https://www.ether.fi/@emi","date":"2026-08-26","likes":43,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2092731640749473861-fx1.jpg"}]},"2091618318385807640":{"text":"Grok Bot is texting my partner a joke + words of endearment every 30 minutes\nI can remotely see the agent from my phone navigating a Linux VPS and sending the message\nOnly took one minute, one prompt to set up. Crazy simple","date":"2026-08-23","likes":24,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2091618318385807640-HQbrxiEXkAAuIrl.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2091618318385807640-HQbrxiIWoAEs0Ra.jpg"}]},"2091232909600436585":{"text":"I’m 15 minutes into Grok Bot and it’s:\n- scanning my email ready to reply whenever an ATOMIX waitlist spot opens up\n- scraping app store reviews and doing sentiment analysis\n- going through and taking screenshots of a full onboarding flow to analyze later","date":"2026-08-22","likes":53},"2095139148352933993":{"text":"I used to rotate between AI subscriptions and found it's best to keep the main frontier models and consistently test all of them as they improve so quickly. Current stack:\n\nHermes (Deepseek V4 Pro) - for routine tasks, it hosts my memory which other LLMs can tap into. Usually accessed from my telegram\nClaude (Fable 5) - for deep research involving hundreds of sources, analysis, strategy, and coding (sometimes I switch to Opus to save on tokens)\nChatGPT (Sol 5.6) - for creative, animations with remotion, and copywriting. Starting to test codex more for coding. I like that ChatGPT browser integration works with Arc too, whereas Claude's doesn't \nGrok (4.6 heavy) - for dense real time X research. I sometimes start here and feed into Fable 5, must have if you work in tech or crypto\nGrok Bot - similar to my hermes usage for routine and personal life upkeep but a more sleek and smooth product experience\nGemini 3.5 Flash - i interface with this model a lot in Google searches, and sometimes use it with my Hermes to save on tokens \n\nModels and AI tools I've used less frequently: \nEleven Labs - voice overs for video creative \nReddit's AI - great for getting Reddit sentiment (like Grok for X) but not as dense\nSuno - music/sound creation \nHiggsfield (Seedance 2.5) - for high fidelity video and AI UGC \nMidjourney - for creating base static creatives that I feed into Seedance or ChatGPT\nNotebook LLM - used it for research before switching full on to Fable 5 and just getting Youtube transcripts ove","date":"2026-09-02","likes":444,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2095139148352933993-fx1.jpg"}]},"2076792346423779473":{"text":"Breaking down the complete process for brand strategy and what went into these 298 slides with @enaraxr tomorrow\nFirst live stream in months! 3 pm cet, 9 am est. If you have questions for her, drop below","date":"2026-07-13","likes":85,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2076792346423779473-HNI_oYyWwAA8gbe.jpg"}]},"2036656960775327912":{"text":"Real marketing use cases AI helped me with this week: \n\n- Retention and cohort analysis: via mcp connected to data lake\n- Competitor research: combo of grok + opus to cover x sentiment, docs, and product\n- Paid media plan creation: used voice in claude, spoke through channels, targeting, and budgets and it produced a sheet \n- Campaign and creative brief creation: similar to paid media plans, just speak to mic \n- Copy refinement: putting drafts into claude with input on desired outcomes, gettint multiple iterations of short and long form copy to review before going live","date":"2026-03-25","likes":147},"1936513690930713037":{"text":"Teacup puppy influencers doing asmr mukbang videos\nVeo 3 to generate\nChatGPT 4o to help with the prompts and characters: Tati Tater Tot, Claudette du Fluff, Beau D. Weenie and Meatball lol","date":"2025-06-21","likes":38,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1936513690930713037-q7kbT-Av12ASujcQ.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1936512696892993536/img/DajpZBrArK8xYWK6.jpg"}]},"1927119621691171035":{"text":"Kaito Yaps vs. Cookie Snaps. What's more effective?\nI compare the two InfoFi platforms based on mindshare measurement and talk through which is better\nWe look at the @sparkdotfi campaign which is the first big snap campaign and see how it compares to others","date":"2025-05-26","likes":230,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1927109992458383361/img/khvtyMMWhVM5lOlj.jpg","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1927109992458383361/img/khvtyMMWhVM5lOlj.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Here are some mindshare breakdowns that I go over in the video between @Cookie3_com and @KaitoAI based on Snaps and Yap campaigns that started on both\n> @sparkdotfi is the first to go live on Cookie and although the mindshare charts on both platforms look similar, it is 2.4x…","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1927119626552381481-Gr59VY7XwAAs5uk.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1927119626552381481-Gr596GmW0AAvyMT.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1927119626552381481-Gr5_gdcWwAAm7kO.jpg"}]}]},"1927701786862789074":{"text":"Part two: What gets you more people talking about you: yaps vs. snaps? \n\nAlso a framework on how to design these mindshare campaigns \n\nthis last video got me 0.66 snaps when showing @sparkfinance and showing their campaign, data dashboard, and some thoughts. Currently ranking #162 out of 4.2k snappers lol","date":"2025-05-28","likes":76,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1927701786862789074-1W-c-R0WGQN46z8f.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1927700700785467392/img/oPZnHzT5WAC5Ok90.jpg"}]},"1871808262020206928":{"text":"How do you actually earn Yap points? I used data to reverse engineer what seems to be working to: \n\n1. show how data can be used to answers questions\n2. hopefully contribute to clarity and see more authentic and interesting takes on my timeline \n\nUsing both Kaito's Yap Dashboard and X native analytics, I looked at the last 7 days and broke down points each day \n\nFirst thing that I noticed was getting 61 yap points on December 21st even though there was 2x less impressions with December 23rd\n\n> 1st insight: it's not just about impressions \n\nI looked into December 21st to see what happened and see if it has something to do with the posts itself, engagers, or something else  \n\nI looked at new follows and # of replies to see if quality engagement had something to do with it\n\n> 2nd insight: yap points can be high even if you have less reposts, less replies, less new follows. There is another qualifier around *what* you post and how \n\nSo what did i actually post that day?\n\nOn the 21st I only wrote one post on how @_kaitoai set a precedent with the surprise genesis nft mint as a saas product, and I tagged 4 friends from the team.\n\nTo isolate this, I know i mentioned Kaito on December 22nd too, the following day. This post had 2x less impressions and 41 points\n\n>3rd insight: tagging @_kaitoai directly seems to help, especially if the team themselves reply back to you (both @sandraleow and @Punk9277 being \"smart followers\") \n\nLastly I looked at the other top day which was December 23rd also at 61 points. This day had no mention of Kaito or other possible companies people are keyword stuffing but did have the most replies all week and decent level reposts \n\nSome of these replies are from \"smart followers\"\n\n> 4th insight: there is some blended qualifier of: \n- *who* replies to you \n- who/what brands you are mentioning \n\nWhat this means for me:\nI'm going to keep posting as is. No need to gamify it, just be myself. I am going to curate my timeline a bit and will be more intentional this week about what posts I reply to based on: \n- if they made me laugh \n- if they taught me something new \n- if they're people i admire and work with \n- real, raw, authentic takes \n\nhappy yapping and merry xmas","date":"2024-12-25","likes":125,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1871808262020206928-GfnzsoTW8AAhTIf.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1871808262020206928-Gfn2MUIXMAAyY7b.png"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1871808262020206928-Gfn7aYBXMAA12I6.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1871808262020206928-Gfn9kIsXIAAICZ_.jpg"}]},"1914319849024606671":{"text":"Alright i'll bite, what even is compute???\n\nHang out with @konyk001, CEO of Gaib and i as i learn: \n•⁠  ⁠cost of building an ai model  \n•⁠  ⁠what's next in ai use cases\n•⁠  ⁠how many GPUs Grok3 is using \n•⁠  ⁠how retail can invest in a new asset class of GPUs using @gaib_ai \n\nCompute is the most precious resource that is powering all of AI... including the editing of this video where ai helped enhanced our voices bc the mics were absolutely not on (i bought them that day and was still learning to use them lol) so that's why we sound like robots","date":"2025-04-21","likes":69,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1914318644969971712/img/Ob4nS96dVGX3tf0R.jpg","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1914318644969971712/img/Ob4nS96dVGX3tf0R.jpg"}]},"1890047985289142661":{"text":"⋆𖦹⊹₊✿⋆ WE VIBE CODE ⋆✿₊ ⊹𖦹⋆\nai made me whole website and snake game in ten minutes!!!!","date":"2025-02-13","likes":138,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1890047985289142661-yhink9_H9ectoNY9.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1890046956510003200/pu/img/HDpAp73x-DE2Lq3N.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"here's the website and game i made in ten minutes i am shooketh lol\ndemo:","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1890048442858373477-GjrM-s_XoAAdCTw.jpg"}]},{"text":"snake game doesn’t work on mobile sorry yall"}]},"1891795292984406270":{"text":"⋆𖦹⊹₊✿⋆ WE VIBE CODE pt. 2 ⋆✿₊ ⊹𖦹⋆\nAI made me a website in 10 minutes of where you can find me at eth denver!!!\ncatch me if you can:","date":"2025-02-18","likes":104,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1891795292984406270-NLJ7erMbtLYv_z0u.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1891708565309751296/pu/img/ViM0yg68FaE3Ffix.jpg"}]},"1886866126824407313":{"text":"Starting a new series called Cozy and Curious where we ask experts about the future, tech, and where the world is going \n\nCome wonder with me about: \n- how quantum computing affects crypto\n- harnessing unlimited compute \n- what happens to bitcoin when 21 million is mined up \n- future of living and working \n- when can i merge myself with ai and talk to aliens\n+ more \n\nPurpose of this is to get some of the most technical, smart minds across tech, ai, crypto to make things easy to understand for all. One hour episodes, live streamed, casual and cozy \n\nFirst episode announced this week\n\nWhat other topics and guests should I have?","date":"2025-02-04","likes":172,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1886866126824407313-db2evT-TiQqMxXwi.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1886866117232091136/img/ISRhWWifCZKLxxfp.jpg"}]},"1836436116628804003":{"text":"Key learnings from this banger presentation from @ekrahm (behind the mind virus of Celestia) on positioning and marketing \n\n1. Positioning is rational, branding is emotional. You need both.\n2. Start with positioning first.\n3. If you don't position, you will be positioned.\n4. Find your differentiation, either within a category or creating a new one.\n5. Four qs for getting to positioning: what is my project, why does it matter, why my project (competitive landscape), why now (timing)?\n6. Successful positioning is a mind virus. It spreads to other communities, tribes, people.\n7. Your brand is what people say about you. It's earned, a prize.\n8. Every brand has some type of archetype (from Carl Jung's studies) and Ekram also categorized some crypto brands. \n9. Not a lot of web2 playbooks on positioning work in web3, it's still a WIP. \n\nSuch an underrated video. I think every marketer should give it a watch","date":"2024-09-18","likes":239,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1836436116628804003-GXxS1FCWIAABD5i.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1836436116628804003-GXxTWntWwAAEvkS.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1836436116628804003-GXxTsmuWcAAn9oc.png"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1836436116628804003-GXxTvlsWMAAfwGI.png"}],"thread":[{"text":"Also, Ekram is joining us live as we learn about building crypto narratives\nCome join"}]},"1808140971181224189":{"text":"Playing around with Runway Gen-3 and other text/image to video ai tools last few days\nRunway Gen-3 is beautifully good. There is a cost though and currently only text-to-video\nHere’s how the tools (Luma, Gen-2) stack up","date":"2024-07-02","likes":7,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1808140971181224189-DNyAIr-Hd2W89Yjw.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1808140884451426304/img/rkGUFi49cotYHRzQ.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Luma (free) with the prompt “this cute baby otter floating on its back playing and juggling with three different colored balls”\nIt’s based off an image I pulled from the internet","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1808141036109099446-mINq_hAKrflG2rMl.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1808140975795232768/img/3xEnWPic_UiRbwKG.jpg"}]},{"text":"Gen-2 with the same exact prompt and image\nAlso free to use","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1808141095626272875-Cn9J7jCk84QGDKAQ.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1808141039837863936/img/lqiZYjq5rWzM0s6X.jpg"}]},{"text":"Gen-3, no image as it’s only text to video for now so prompt only\nThe only one that got the juggle","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1808141166610726980-y3DAfYkpicHqb0jm.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1808141098738765826/img/gDW5CbTtEUlxiDFC.jpg"}]},{"text":"Very fun. The prompt for the jellyfish was most specific\nExcited to keep playing and seeing what comes from our creative department","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1808141175284543743-GRfO0GyWgAA7TM6.jpg"}]}]},"1685536068328722432":{"text":"Want to learn marketing?\nMake $ online or get a remote job?\nThere’s a ton of information on YouTube, Twitter, blogs… it’s overwhelming\nI’ve gotten a few dms like this.\nHere’s a list of high-quality marketing resources I send back and recommend:","date":"2023-07-30","likes":24,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1685536068328722432-F2Q6HQ6WgAAPwPr.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Starting point: Identify which marketing domains resonate and are interesting to you to learn.\nRead: Brian Balfour’s “How to Become a UA (user acquisition) Expert” can help identify what you’re interested in, and links to many other high quality blogs: …"}]},"1062947052101857280":{"text":"Reading books is the real life version of collecting mushrooms in Super Mario","date":"2018-11-15","likes":2290},"1881423550298607917":{"text":"So many crypto companies say marketers are hard to find and at the same time a lot of marketers are looking for work\nTomorrow @jkey_eth and I will cover how to get into @Safaryclub and how to best position yourself to get hired\nLive stream video with q&a, come join us","date":"2025-01-20","likes":246,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1881423550298607917-Ghwnh0tXgAIPXEY.jpg"}]},"1982784231806742937":{"text":"Get Hired in Crypto Marketing (Q4 2025 edition)\n\n- Current state of crypto jobs (there's more marketers and content creators now than Q1 when I did a similar stream)\n- On positioning yourself: defining what you're great at that matches what a company needs\n- Marketing yourself: how and where to show up\n- What we look for at Hype when hiring\n- How to cold dm + other tips\n\nAlso found a few companies hiring in the last 24 hours of making this deck including @KhanAbbas201 for a CT Lead for the EF, @ldf_gm at @LayerZero_Core, @eden_ for @doublezero and @redstone_defi for a new cmo (lol)\n\nShouted them all out in the slides. Huge thanks to @yzolotukhina and @shefiorg for organizing this <3","date":"2025-10-27","likes":562,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1982783174871531520/img/bh9duUG7h1duqVA9.jpg","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1982783174871531520/img/bh9duUG7h1duqVA9.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"If you’re looking for your next role in crypto, or looking to hire marketing and technical talent, chat with our @talent_hype team"}]},"2059019371163291860":{"text":"Just finished a hiring round for our growth team. A ton of dms and resumes flooded in from this post\n\nI know there’s a lot of people looking for their next career chapter. I was reflecting on what I signals I use to filter applications and invite to first round interviews: \n\nBucket A: Specialist in a specific channel that is hands on (e.g. performance marketing, lifecycle marketing) \n- Firstly requires a clear view of OKRs and how to achieve them to know what roles to build around  \n- Some knowledge in how time intensive each speciality is and if it requires dedicated talent doing it full time, or a generalist type (this is changing with AI) \n- Should be visible in a candidates resume with quantifiable results \n- As a candidate, you should also reflect knowledge of the skill with the exact tool stacks you’ve used in your cv \n\nBucket B: Generalist with domain expertise \n- For example, a marketing lead or growth marketer who wore multiple hats but worked at a competitor, breakout app, or company in similar category \n- Requires awareness of and identifying breakout companies, competitors, similar cos in your category (some carry more weight) \n- Ideally comes with some edge based on that exact vertical (existing relationships, knowledge in best converting channels, angles, geos etc) \n- When applying as a candidate, highlight companies you’ve worked at that are most similar to the job with call outs on how you helped them grow \n\nOther signals I look for: \n- Ability to position themselves concisely in cold dms \n- How metrics and responsibilities are framed in cv\n- Existing owned distribution: do they have any social channels or media they’ve built up themselves \n- Proactivity and grit signaled by any entrepreneurial experience \n- AI-native (usually more deeply sourced in interview) \n\nReference checks are also important in key hiring decisions, if you’re an applicant, expect this to happen \n\nThis means dream hires are someone who has a combination of both buckets and some of the bonus signals too. They have channel or tactic specialties they’ve built up over the years, have executed them in a company in a similar vertical that has proven breakout growth, and come with existing distribution and relationships","date":"2026-05-25","likes":200},"1886495008569675940":{"text":"things i’d look into to become a better crypto marketer (onchain edition) \n\n> check defi llama for recent surges in tvl, reverse engineer how the protocol did it across coms, incentives, and distribution \n> review recent successful tges and note down their tokenomics \n> read marketing proposals on governance forums \n\non top of marketing fundamentals, of course","date":"2025-02-03","likes":264},"1986716841201336412":{"text":"What do brands look for in “kols” and creators? Some slides from my presentation yesterday. \n\nUltimately it depends on the company but general gist is whatever drives fees and revenue\n\nTrading platforms: drive volumes, new signups, deposits \nNeobanks/crypto cards: app downloads, KYC, deposits\nDeFi protocols: tvl, swap/borrow/lend volumes, wallet connects \nChains: bridged volumes, unique wallet connects, dapp usage volumes \n\nWhen brands look at content creators and “kols,” they’re looking to leverage the trust these creators have built with their audience to acquire new users \n\nThe more trust a “kol” or creator has with their audience, the more likely their audience will convert and skip steps in the funnel\n\nTo better explain it, I used the crypto marketing funnel I made 2.5 years ago and wow, a lot has changed. The landscape is so much more fruitful between infra, middleware, dapps. There’s no one size fits all. Discord is used a lot less, infofi platforms came in this year while questing sunset. ICOs came back in form of pre deposits and crowdsales. Co-marketing with partners helps gtm in a composable landscape. Goes to show things change so fast in crypto and there’s no such thing as a crypto marketing playbook. \n\nFull recording is in my highlights","date":"2025-11-07","likes":125,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1986716841201336412-G5I8S2jXAAADUPV.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1986716841201336412-G5I8S2iXcAA6qET.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1986716841201336412-G5I8S2iWQAAWxqm.jpg"}]},"1791435120596996195":{"text":"After hiring 15+ people since the start of this year and conducting 80+ interviews, I'm reflecting on our T-Shaped Web3 Marketer framework. \n\n1. Just having agency or brand experience in tech, consumer, product is not enough.  The people that thrive at Hype live onchain. They are immersed into crypto culture. They mint, trade, stake, farm, claim. They spend time on crypto Twitter, Hey, Warpcast. They're in 237482 telegram groups and discords. They also understand the nuances of crypto culture which brings me to...\n\n2. The \"Web3 Knowledge\" piece is getting more segmented as the space matures. Specifically at Hype, most of our work is in bringing DeFi protocols, ecosystems, and dev infra to market. The type of knowledge for growth in these segments tends to be a bit more technical. Consumer crypto, meme coins, and say, a modular restaking protocol all attract different types of users with their own culture-bubbles online. \n\n3. I would add in innovation and adaptability to our framework. Someone who is living and breathing onchain culture will see how often the metas change. \nYear 1 for me at Hype was a lot of L1 ecosystems, nfts, games. It birthed our DevRel teams as we quickly learned we needed to know how to connect with builders. We did a lot of whitelisting campaigns. \nYear 2 was dev infra, we did a lot of launches in a bear market which was less noisy \nToday and in Q1 2024, there are many launches and TGEs. \n\nThe space's metas change - LSTs/LRTs are hot, DePin, memecoins are in now\n\nMarketing metas in web3 also change (and change fast) - airdrop farming was big.. watch it move towards retrospective airdrops and other reward mechanisms after users get desensitized. Brand marketing will continue to crush this year as projects try to stand out in all the noise. \n\nAll this to say, it's exciting to see the space continuing to mature to a point where \"web3 marketer\" is a vague term. We are still very early and far from PMF (unless you're a stablecoin, exchange, wallet) which means the audience targeted is a niche and requires deep understanding. IF you are someone that lives and breathes onchain, please dm me as we are always looking for the best to join our team.","date":"2024-05-17","likes":179},"2088274956211593457":{"text":"The generalist growth/marketing role in crypto does not exist anymore. \n\nThis makes an onboarding funnel byway of a single course difficult. I used to make a lot more \"crypto growth marketing\" content in the last years and have reviewed hundreds of gtm cvs in multiple hiring cycles when the industry was more premature. These days, I'm studying for the FINRA.\n\nCrypto is becoming concentrated in the following:\n1. Onchain finance (effectively, finance - as the rails become more invisible)\n2. Market infrastructure\n3. Trading platforms \n\nWith many companies folding or aggregating, combined with current market conditions, most will head hunt specialized talent and go with seniors over juniors.\n\nOnchain finance is a broad category that is an analog to traditional capital markets. This means an increased demand in expertise coming from finance and banking. Market infrastructure is all the piping needed to power this. This is entirely B2B. The main audiences a growth or marketing role would be targeting in a more mature crypto space include: \n- retail and consumer traders \n- SMEs \n- financial institutions \n- family offices \n- trading desks \n- asset managers \n- other company's in the space  \n\nThe retail and consumer segment is hyper-competitive. Power laws apply to the largest exchanges, trading platforms, and neobanks. These companies source talent from other high growth web2 consumer apps or competitors. For trading platforms, you'd want to target power traders as they drive most of your revenue. This is primarily B2B, right there with the rest of the audiences on the list. These relationships and knowledge in each segment's pain points, current solutions, and technical prowess come with specialized experience that accrues over time.","date":"2026-08-14","likes":150},"1993137695145533533":{"text":"Crypto Marketing Trends & Predictions: 2026 and Beyond\n\nCrypto moves fast. Attention spans are short. Trends are coming and dying with tighter life cycles. The keynote I shared for g(t)m con 1 last Sunday, November 16th includes observations and learnings","date":"2025-11-25","likes":773,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1993137695145533533-cover.jpg"}]},"1921894825944658090":{"text":"Getting the first 100 people who actually care (even if you are shy or hate ct)\n\nThis is not about Galxe, Zealy, Layer3 or questing tools\n\nOur VP of Growth @glitch_ will be sharing his keynote with me this wednesday, 9 am pst/12 pm est/6 pm cet \n\nJoin the live stream, we'll be answering Qs and also going over the internal community funnel canvas we use at @hypepartners","date":"2025-05-12","likes":278,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1921894825944658090-GqvvdklXUAAmb6p.jpg"}]},"1919764012553613578":{"text":"What's the current state of crypto growth? We need to talk. \n\nHere's the keynote I delivered at Growth Summit:\n- \"token price is the best marketing\" ...but why is that and should it be? \n- why are there 6942 new metas every other month?\n- What's an example of a project that did it right? \n- where is the industry headed?\n- when cynicism is at all time highs, what can you do?","date":"2025-05-06","likes":226,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1919761223555358720/img/HQdmpbjyPP6WXNC7.jpg","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1919761223555358720/img/HQdmpbjyPP6WXNC7.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Source on 1.8 million tokens dying already in 2025 and us not even being halfway through yet lol is by @ShaunPaulLee here:"}]},"1899900098202550681":{"text":"User Acquisition & Marketing Foundations for Crypto Companies\n\nMarketing can be overwhelming. From choosing the right channels, to messaging, to coordination. Should you invest in an event? Start an ambassador program? What should the hackathon incentives be?","date":"2025-03-12","likes":684,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1899900098202550681-cover.jpg"}]},"1861696138812051488":{"text":"We’re excited to welcome @emilylai, CMO at @hypepartners, to the #IBW2024 Conference! 🪷\n\nWith 8+ years of marketing experience across e-commerce, DTC, SaaS, and apps, Emily has been a pro-crypto advocate since 2015 and has dedicated the past 3 years to full-time crypto marketing. As the driving force behind Hype, the leading onchain super agency, she’s shaping the future of marketing in Web3. 🙌\n\nDon’t miss the opportunity to hear from one of the industry's top marketing experts at IBW2024! 🔥","date":"2024-11-27","likes":212,"author":"IBWofficial","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1861696138812051488-fx1.jpg"}]},"1845853616545939779":{"text":"\"Founder Branding is important\"\n•Emily Lai•\n\nI just realised I've been sleeping on Founder Branding 🤦🏽‍♀️\n\nLearning so much from @emilylai talk about 'Marketing in Crypto' during the @OctantApp accelerator programme!\n\nLearning and applying so much with this on @BitsaveProtocol","date":"2024-10-14","likes":40,"author":"_karlagod","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1845853616545939779-fx1.jpg"}]},"1838301600663867460":{"text":"Thrilled to announce Emily Lai as a speaker!\n\nEmily is the CMO at @hypepartners, the leading onchain super agency.\n\nShe has 8+ years in marketing, starting in performance marketing for both consumer goods, SAAS and apps.\n\nShe’s been a crypto enthusiast since 2016 and has worked in crypto marketing for the last 3 years.\n\nExcited for our cohort, with @emilylai leading the growth marketing sessions!","date":"2024-09-23","likes":29,"author":"OctantApp","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1838301600663867460-fx1.jpg"}]},"1797677263510757859":{"text":"Its been over a year since I shared our web3 marketing funnel \n\nA lot has changed since then..\n1. We haven't ran any paid campaigns this year, it's all been fairly organic distribution that is community driven\n2. Crew3 and L2E platforms have evolved so much in the last 12 months\n3. A lot of Q1 2024 was airdrop farming campaigns (which has also now become overplayed - see my recent post to expand on that)  \n\nHere's how the web3 marketing funnel looks internally at @hypepartners with some of the biggest projects in the space: \n1. It's bespoke. We tailor it to every project as funnel varies based on vertical, stage, and goals \n2. You'll see there is a reverse funnel... its now an hourglass shape. That's because entering the community *is* the conversion point, but once a member has joined a community there is a whole other user flow to keep engage and retain \n\nS/o to our VP of Growth (@glitch_), our roster our badass growth strategists, and full team bringing our GTM strategies to life. Has been nonstop the last 8 months as we consistently iterate and innovate to bring some of crypto's best projects to scale.","date":"2024-06-03","likes":79,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1797677263510757859-fx1.jpg"}]},"1623077710980415489":{"text":"Why is web3 marketing so hard?\nIt's not. It's complex.\nBehold: the marketing \"funnel\"\nFunnel in quotes because it's not so straight forward...","date":"2023-02-07","likes":112,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1623077710980415489-FoZPErjWAAEc1ta.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"At it's core, web3 marketing is\n1. Part content media empire\n2. Part community marketing & management\n3. Sometimes developer marketing\nThere's feedback loops all around between content + community, community + product, and product + content\nA lot of KPIS to track!"},{"text":"To make it even more complex, there is a spectrum of content across multiple channels between\nBrand safe, pure meme culture\nThen a spectrum of targeting from\nenthusiasts, traders, developers\nA spectrum of touch points both horizontally and vertically"},{"text":"A project needs resourcing around\n1. Talent: both brains and passion. And A LOT of it. (Teams tend to lot larger compared to an ecom marketing)\n2. Analytics/BI/Tooling: save cost on inefficiencies in the complex funnel, scale faster\n3. Time: which requires runway $"},{"text":"Talent is the biggest chunk. You’ll need a team on every “layer” of the funnel: content creators, social managers, community managers, campaign strategist…\nIt’s the daily grind at @hypepartners\nWe’re also developing our own dashboard for web3 growth:"},{"text":"+ tagged some tools we’re currently testing or wanting to test (wink) with our web3 clients\n@layer3xyz @crew3xyz @guildxyz @chainvine_xyz @RaleonHQ @AhoyConnect @blaze_ai\nAny other recommended web3 tools for growth? Please dm or share 😄"}]},"2095510628865593684":{"text":"Website updated. Wispr Flow and Claude. \n\nhttps://defi-native.ai","date":"2026-09-03","likes":38,"author":"defi_native_ai","media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/2095510628865593684-fx1.mp4","poster":"media/2095510628865593684-fx1-poster.jpg"}]},"2095549760631443716":{"text":"Hit $1,130,000 in ARR (lol). Annualizers, assemble.\n\nThe story of defi-native: \n1. I wanted to learn more about onchain vaults + yield. \n2. I used AI to help learn.\n3. This led to learning more about tradfi, cefi, and traditional markets as building blocks.\n3. AI was not always accurate, so I fed it 100+ transcripts, docs, books, resources. \n4. I turned that into an \"Onchain Capital Markets Bible,\" a 217 page book. \n5. To use AI properly to learn, it needs instructions so I made a skill.md it could read. The book was fed back to it, enriched with more APIs, files, and docs. I structured it in a way that based on the prompt, a model knows what to check and fetch. \n6. I shared the defi-native skill here on X, someone made a token on bankr and directed fees at me. \n7. I've since used some of those fees to airdrop back to early holders, secure a domain, purchase inference, and build a website. \n\nThis is now a side project that helps me continually learn what AI is capable of and run some growth experiments while deepening knowledge of defi and finance.  The skill is consistently updated, already has one external contribution (thank you!), and is free for anyone to use :)\n\nWebsite: Wispr Flow + Fable 5 + lots of design skills \nImages: 5.6 Sol \nVideo: 5.6 Sol + Remotion skills\nAirdrop: Fable 5, distributed via Bankr\nCopy: mainly me","date":"2026-09-03","likes":170,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2095549760631443716-fx1.jpg"}]},"2094480103463899494":{"text":"Really cool to get feedback and see people using @defi_native_ai, a skill I made to make your Claude, ChatGPT, Grok Bot defi native!\n\nI use AI daily to accelerate my learning. But I found it to have gaps with domain specific expertise including finance. It can be over confident with answers and lead one astray. This defi-native skill is loaded with context and structured to answer any questions on vault strategies, yield, crypto market microstructure, curators, defi primitives, onchain private credit + much, much more\n\nUnlike most AI skills or agents, this does not execute trades for you. I built it for myself to help learn and am continually adding to it. The latest version includes onchain options, due diligence guides from curators, and better structure of how APIs are called  \n\nThere was a token launched from @bankrbot community. I don't own any of it. I've used some of the claimed fees to: \n- buy a domain \n- build a website \n- get X premium badge\n- verify on dexscreener \n- buy llm tokens \n- airdrop back to holders (bankrbot is an ai that allows your to do this from a prompt! coinfello also can help you execute onchain) \n\nIf you use it, let me know what you think and how it can be improved \n\nfirst time launching a website with claude code from zero, insane you can do this in an hour","date":"2026-08-31","likes":67,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2094480103463899494-fx1.jpg"}]},"2094132631478698379":{"text":"also used the $100 LLM credits from the @bankrbot team to send some of the fees claimed to all holders:) pretty cool it can do that directly from the app\n\nmake sure to update to the latest defi-skill here (v.1.6.4), or try it out: https://github.com/emlai/defi-native-skill","date":"2026-08-30","likes":15,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2094132631478698379-fx1.jpg"}]},"2093449036401705349":{"text":"I built a skill to make your ai defi native.\n\nCrypto is turning into finance on new rails. To upskill, I've been studying for my FINRA and kept noticing how even the latest models are not crypto native and don't have a full picture of what's being built onchain\n\nThis one skill is distilled from 6,000+ pages of books on the history of banking, conference and podcast transcripts, industry reports, and is structured so your agent knows which docs to pull and what to check across 90+ protocols, infra, curators and more \n\nNow you can actually ask your agent \"where does the yield come from\" and get an exact breakdown along with risks and opportunities\n\nWorks with claude, cursor, codex, any agent that reads skills. Lmk if you want to test it and improve it!","date":"2026-08-28","likes":194,"author":"emilylai"},"2093538609827631270":{"text":"Published my first public github repo today: a skill for any AI that gives it capital markets, onchain finance, and defi understanding\n\nI made it for myself to learn all the layers of onchain finance. It does a great breaking down yield strategies, vaults, risks, infra stack, and various markets and asset types\n\nTry it here: https://github.com/emlai/defi-native-skill\n\nSince then, there's been a random token launched in honor(?) of it on @bankrbot . The team (+ this skill) has been really helpful in understanding what's going on lol. Unsure where to go from here with it but i'll keep pushing updates to the repo as needed. I'm personally using the skill every day to learn\n\nGeneral purpose models, even the frontier ones miss gaps and tend to be overconfident in output. I've experienced this often using ai for specific marketing and growth functions. Directing context and clear instructions in a skill helps a lot. If you're learning about a protocol or assessing a defi opportunity, let me know if you use it and have feedback. If you have deep expertise in finance, banking, capital markets, please test it and let me know if there's gaps in output i can patch","date":"2026-08-29","likes":149,"author":"emilylai","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2093538609827631270-fx1.jpg"}]},"2094132628458803417":{"text":"New update to defi-native, the skill that makes your AI an expert on capital markets and onchain finance\n\nAdded 119+ new sources and better structure with which APIs to call based on prompts.\n\nNow you AI will know all about STORMM, tokenized stock/memecoin pairs, onchain options, how curators size risk, and more","date":"2026-08-30","likes":60,"author":"emilylai"},"1909612696674124050":{"text":"Every person I \"onboarded\" onchain has already bought crypto \n\nOnboarded in quotes because crypto IS mainstream. These are the platforms my friends and exes have used to buy it: \n- Coinbase\n- Binance \n- Revolut \n- Trade Republic \n- One friend i live onboarded even bought the btc etf \n\nWhat this means is the value for the end consumer beyond holding it as a financial asset like stocks/bonds is not conveyed or felt enough for them to connect wallet (or even get one)","date":"2025-04-08","likes":114},"1902350737218146573":{"text":"TWO biggest blockers to crypto onboarding (what i learned live onboarding four people in the 30 days) \n\nLACK OF DISCOVERABILITY: There is no centralized app store or library, and everyone is biased. It makes this overwhelming:\n- Choosing a wallet \n- Choosing a chain \n- Choosing apps: dexs, games, socialfi, bridges \n\nA beginner will likely go to google and not X. This leads to scam phishing sites and outdated information. Even on X, you need a lot of discernment since everyone is biased and pushing their wallet/chain/dapp as the best, even if thats untrue\n\nWORD SALAD: Imagine explaining this to beginners: \n- Slippage and why\n- Gas and why you need it \n- ETH vs. wETH vs. stETH \n- USDT vs. USDC vs. DAI vs. etc etc \n- Where does the yield come from \n- Bridging and staking \n- Whale\n- \"Switch network\"/ \"Wrong network\" \n- RPCs\n- Testnets and faucets\n\nOh wait, I did see this live. \n\"What do you think a whale means?\" \n\"A large mammal in the ocean?\"\n\nOne has to be soooo motivated to get past all this friction","date":"2025-03-19","likes":338},"1894551182242451967":{"text":"Normie onboarding another normie to crypto LIVE (ETHDenver)","date":"2025-02-26","likes":83,"thread":[{"text":"Context: I onboarded @Mumufengg 7 days ago and asked her to onboard two people who have never been onchain: Steve and Lauren. I’m here to facilitate to make sure no one gets rugged\nWe had them go through\n- @pumpdotfun\n- @jokerace_io\n- @rodeodotclub\n- @aave\n- @Highlight_xyz…"}]},"1893547624764223503":{"text":"Her first day onchain and i had @shayyydz test 10 dapps per your recs \n\n16:40 - @jokerace_io \n21:45 - @bebop_dex (thank you for the gas <3) \n28:15 - @zora \n32:22 - @scribblfun \n33:50 - @LeatherBTC \n37:50 - @pumpdotfun \n42:20 - @defiapp \n50:38 - @BetSwirl (thank you for the free bets <3) \n1:00:35- @aave \n1:04:50 - @vaultsfyi + @bebop_dex to swap and stake in @MorphoLabs \n1:11:57 - recap \n\nForget onboarding the next billion. Onboard one person.","date":"2025-02-23","likes":80},"1892157681257078845":{"text":"What crypto is really like for someone who has never been onchain and has only ever bought Bitcoin/Ethereum on centralized exchanges\nYes, I have her test pump dot fun too...","date":"2025-02-19","likes":121,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1892157681257078845-YQyBuG7gfBgz1WVi.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1892081704191524865/pu/img/9g-b3NhbwJORxCuR.jpg"}]},"1834538076674163126":{"text":"Helped a friend onboard yesterday to a non custodial crypto debit card, so she can make payments in crypto \n\n*Aha moment* was oh wow my wallet is my own bank and I can switch my debit card between multiple wallets? And this same wallet can also connect to exchanges for swaps? \n\n*brotha ew* moment was all the steps for getting the wallet, get stables there, needing native token gas fees to transfer stables, and checking to make sure both links aren’t scams and you’re on the right chain. Shoutout to gas stations I didn’t know those existed until yesterday. You can directly swap in stables to get the native gas token without having to buy it or have someone send it to you \n\nUX is much better this cycle, still some ways to go","date":"2024-09-13","likes":116},"1901983349784092752":{"text":"The companies bold enough to come on our crypto marketing roast today 🔥\nWe will go live at 2 pm est, 7 pm cet:","date":"2025-03-18","likes":89,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1901983349784092752-GmUyyarWAAATtdL.jpg"}]},"1887933485035225225":{"text":"Get your socials roasted 🔥\nThe one and only @AlexOnchain is joining @reka_eth and i on ep 4 of our crypto marketing roast\nWednesday, february 12th at 10 am pst, 7 pm cet\nWant to come on? Let us know below. Brand or personal pages welcome","date":"2025-02-07","likes":161,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1887933485035225225-cA-WU2FbLaO2ltnw.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1887932957492490240/pu/img/L1_zNeSXL9vemq3V.jpg"}]},"1881671688112246921":{"text":"A presidential marketing roast with special guests @naruto11eth who can flame your tech/docs/product and @RahulDesignWeb3 who can grill your design \n\nLive-streamed, raw feedback, free advice for dapps, marketing campaigns, and websites. Come join episode 3  with @reka_eth and I\n\nLink to get roasted below \nThursday, Jan 23rd 10am est, 4pm cet, 8:30pm ist","date":"2025-01-21","likes":143,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1881671688112246921-pyMdM1WfSlzyntIE.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1881670446602465280/pu/img/C1ftO-nxlxTSoANW.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Sign up to get roasted here:\nEpisode 1:\nEpisode 2:"}]},"1868961934491762770":{"text":"Marketing roast part 2: live feedback on your campaign, product, or website \n\nwe won’t look at anything until we go live so it’ll be raw first impressions\n\nhigh speed, 3-5 minutes per project, one hour total \n\ntune in this thursday, dec 19th, 12 pm cet / 7 pm hkt to watch \n\nsign up to get “roasted” (in quotes bc it ends up being wholesome): https://forms.gle/YFL2fRXy9kf5eFTM7","date":"2024-12-17","likes":140,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1868961934491762770-BjrOnUdlp2EuvKj6.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1868961865235308544/img/1eKg5_YeFfaK2EON.jpg"}]},"1853878703920410926":{"text":"free marketing advice and roast (with love)\ncome on stream and show @reka_eth and i your website, product, or socials. get raw feedback, live\ntomorrow, nov 6th, 10 am est/4 pm cet\ncomment if you're in","date":"2024-11-05","likes":190,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1853878703920410926-pfjnU-JmuuLG5erc.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1853875659195461632/pu/img/JisYgWhTjkdAOgHi.jpg"}]},"1807113908173308269":{"text":"Thinking of doing more shares of failed side projects (I have a lot of them)\nMy first dropshipping store\nmy first whitelabeling store\nThe 2-3 blogs I’ve shut down\nGetting product samples but never going live\nProbably a few more, been failing (and also winning) for a decade+","date":"2024-06-29","likes":23},"1806644072444047692":{"text":"One of my many failed projects included a crypto affiliate blog where I wrote about Bitcoin and how to get started. Throwback to 2017: \n\nIt peaked at 2000+ users in December 2017, all organic  traffic and seo (I did nothing to optimize it) and continued to get organic traffic until I killed it off end of 2019. \n\nI'm too embarrassed to share the domain lol (and it's now gone) but was a mixture of blog articles like how to get started with your hard wallet, why you should trade on GDAX (before it was renamed to Coinbase Pro), future of crypto, and what it means for the world. \n\nHere's one of the flow charts I dug up - many of these are 2+ cycles ago:  \n\nBack then I also was exploring and writing about utilities beyond payments. Tokenized loyalty points, tokenized shares... this was before NFTS blew up. Crazy to see how the space evolved. \n\nThe blog mainly monetized by organic seo traffic and affiliate revenue for Coinbase signups ($10 worth of BTC each signup), Trezor, and Ledger purchases. \n\nBig reason I chalk this one up as a failure? I just stopped writing. I made the brand a bit too personal and didn't anonymize myself as it was getting traction. So now fast forward 7 years later and I can laugh at this pie chart I put in the \"About Me\" page:","date":"2024-06-28","likes":27,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1806644072444047692-GRJ7GnmWsAABKK4.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1806644072444047692-GRJ78qlWcAAaDGZ.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1806644072444047692-GRJ8Q12WIAA1vAw.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1806644072444047692-GRJ9IbKWwAEAKQh.jpg"}]},"2082489035147161837":{"text":"who can connect me to someone i can commission these tables from","date":"2026-07-29","likes":38,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2082489035147161837-HOZ8vHFWIAERQce.jpg"}]},"2067340048735801723":{"text":"bought a new pair on eBay for $100\nshot on google glass:","date":"2026-06-17","likes":114,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/2067340048735801723-HLCqy36WYAEA2cB.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2067340048735801723-HLCqy4DWwAA4c0U.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2067340048735801723-HLCqy5QWAAA7Qvn.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/2067340048735801723-HLCqy4FXEAAvOlM.jpg"}]},"1977155131964899383":{"text":"2025 meta rayban on left vs. 2013 google glass","date":"2025-10-11","likes":2,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1977155131964899383-G3BEHRAbwAAXRwn.jpg"}]},"1977052827366441449":{"text":"update","date":"2025-10-11","likes":381,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1977052827366441449-G2_nETzbIAA8aM2.jpg"}]},"1974377280299483344":{"text":"came to eBay to look at vintage digital cameras, left with this pair of google glass for $100 instead lol","date":"2025-10-04","likes":24,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1974377280299483344-G2Zlq5vWYAAZAV_.jpg"}]},"1834679977968566680":{"text":"The air fryer is the 2nd best invention of all time, after air conditioning and before the iPhone","date":"2024-09-13","likes":57,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1834679977968566680-GXYXtcPWgAAJhnr.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1834679977968566680-GXYXtcMXcAA-uYw.jpg"}]},"1489658457716264960":{"text":"A three part story on what might be the best innovation I’ve seen yet. You get a mini travel tissue pack with each toilet paper roll","date":"2022-02-04","likes":3,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1489658457716264960-FKxUds4WUAQg00H.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1489658457716264960-FKxUds9XoAcZ0tO.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1489658457716264960-FKxUds5XwAIGGgr.jpg"}]},"1843356431099277458":{"text":"imagine post devcon diving\nbd-free environment. no wifi, no cell service, no onboarding me to your perp dex (if you can do it underwater, congrats, ill use it for life)\njust coral and bubbles","date":"2024-10-07","likes":73,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1843356431099277458-GZTq5loWwAADdKP.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1843356431099277458-GZTq5leXIAA_uRb.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1843356431099277458-GZTq5ldXYAAi1hu.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1843356431099277458-GZTq5lbXUAAFo6F.jpg"}]},"1673163588582666240":{"text":"Hi, was off grid hiking some Inca trails for the last 4 days\nWhat’d I miss? Something about a submarine,  coup?\nA baby alpaca vid here to offset any doom and gloom","date":"2023-06-26","likes":17,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1673163588582666240-gHAwNVThLz3pHa74.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/1673163467254005764/img/Qa6M7uzb4xI6IrJ4.jpg"}]},"1513396246647431171":{"text":"My quads are very sore\nOnly hit two trees and ran one over today","date":"2022-04-11","likes":7,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1513396246647431171-Z9dTqDg5vEmAxqIe.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1513395980590329859/pu/img/dqADgrdhIeX3Wotg.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"In all seriousness 360 cameras are crazy. I used an Insta360 One X2. One of the editing features uses AI to track me while making the selfie stick invisible\nMilitary always gets tech first… just thinking about nano drones with 360 cams, or even 360 cams for public surveillance"}]},"1402219054765547522":{"text":"You forget about whales dumping the market when you’re swimming with sharks","date":"2021-06-08","likes":1,"media":[{"t":"video","src":"media/1402219054765547522-OuwR_YEcZdtq1IdC.mp4","poster":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1402219006015143937/pu/img/bEmhmvIRgw3Jq8O5.jpg"}],"thread":[{"text":"Overall, a gentle reminder to forget about the pseudo-digital reality time to time by living in the denser-physical reality\nHug a tree, drink some water, pet a dog, smell a flower","media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1402219072708771841-E3WuzbsVgAYHyGU.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1402219072708771841-E3WuzbpUUAAm47Q.jpg"}]}]},"1317883308840079361":{"text":"Salted egg yolk is no secret in the Asian community.\nBack in NYC, we found a place with salted egg yolk mooncakes and lava cake.\nIn Denver, we got salted egg yolk lobster.\nBut the delicious, OG salted egg yolk chips and fish skin snacks are very rare... for now","date":"2020-10-18","likes":0,"media":[{"t":"photo","src":"media/1317883308840079361-EkoP4K8VoAAdR3b.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1317883308840079361-EkoP4MVVgAMZ5X8.jpg"},{"t":"photo","src":"media/1317883308840079361-EkoP4O6VkAEFGfL.jpg"}]}};
